h44jh8P":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/WeFitIn-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-230741\nsed -n 358,371p API.md | cut -c1-220; sed -n 460,478p API.md | cut -c1-220; sed -n 352,357p API.md | cut -c1-200; sed -n 550,566p API.md | cut -c1-200; sed -n 577,603p API.md | cut -c1-200; sed -n 1886,1900p API.md | cut -c1-200; sed -n 2116,2122p API.md | cut -c1-200; sed -n 4733,4740p API.md|cut -c1-200; grep -n \"interface BurstOptions\" -A8 API.md </dev/null | cut -c1-160; grep -n \"interface TweenOptions\" -A8 API.md </dev/null | cut -c1-160; grep -n \"type Ease\\b\" -A4 API.md </dev/null | cut -c1-300; grep -n \"class ContactShadow\" -A9 API.md </dev/null | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"interface TrailOptions\" -A8 API.md </dev/null | cut -c1-160;  grep -n \"^### buildModel\\|interface ModelBuild\" -A12 API.md </dev/null | sed -n 1,22p | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"addModelColliders\" API.md </dev/null | head -2 | cut -c1-200","description":"Read settings, camera, effect and model build API details","timeout":30000}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SSqDWx7YtZagyWVh44jh8P","type":"tool_result","content":"### interface PlayerSettings\n\nThe player's settings: the standard picture and engine options every game gets, as plain data\n(sound is the AudioManager's, which keeps its own volumes). A field left out is the game's own\nchoice; a field set is the player's and wins over it. `engine.settings` holds them, applies\nthem, saves them per game and shows them in the settings panel (the ⚙ button).\n\n- `look?: string`: A LOOK_PRESETS name. Left out: the look the game gives each level.\n- `pixelArt?: boolean`: Pixel art (the pixel pass), or false for smooth 3D (render mode `raw`).\n- `pixelSize?: 'fine' | 'chunky'`: The art resolution: `fine` (the game's, 480×270 by default) or `chunky` (two thirds of it: bigger pixels).\n- `quality?: QualityOption`: Shadow and light quality: a level, or `auto` (the device's).\n- `fps?: number`: Frame cap: 60, 30, or 0 for the display's own rate.\n- `debugInfo?: boolean`: The debug panel: frame rate, camera, GPU errors and the game's status.\n\n### class Settings\n\n`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\nsets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\nsaved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\nsettings panel.\n\n- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n- `readonly key: string | null`\n- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n- `get isOpen: boolean`\n- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n- `open(): void`\n- `close(): void`\n- `toggle(): void`\n\n### PIXEL_SIZES\n\n```ts\nconst PIXEL_SIZES: readonly [\"fine\", \"chunky\"]\n```\n\n### interface CameraConfig\n\n- `preset?: CameraPreset`\n- `zoom?: number`: Zoom factor, 1 = preset default, >1 = closer. Ignored by `first`.\n- `minZoom?: number`\n- `maxZoom?: number`\n- `viewHeight?: number`: Ortho presets: visible world height at zoom 1.\n- `pitch?: number`: iso: degrees below horizon / around Y.\n- `yaw?: number`\n- `fov?: number`: Perspective presets: vertical field of view in degrees.\n- `distance?: number`: third: orbit distance at zoom 1.\n- `position?: [number, number, number]`: fixed: camera position and look-at target.\n- `target?: [number, number, number]`\n- `projection?: 'perspective' | 'ortho'`: fixed/free: projection.\n- `stiffness?: number`: Follow smoothing; higher is snappier.\n\n### type CameraPreset\n### class CameraRig\n\nBase rig: owns the three.js camera, zoom and the ground-plane movement basis.\n\n- `new CameraRig(config: CameraConfig)`\n- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera | PerspectiveCamera`\n- `readonly focus: Vector3`: World point the rig is centred on (used for shadow framing).\n- `zoom: number`\n- `readonly minZoom: number`\n- `readonly maxZoom: number`\n- `readonly zoomable: boolean`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n- `readonly hidesTarget: boolean`: First person hides the player model.\n- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n- `controlsCharacter: boolean`: False while the free camera is flying (input drives the camera, not the player).\n- `snap: boolean`: Pixel-snap the camera (ortho only).\n- `aspect: number`: Viewport aspect (width / height), following the art resolution (see `setAspect`).\n- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts\n- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n- `setAspect(aspect: number): void`: Match the art resolution's aspect (adaptive framing changes it with the screen). `update()` calls this from `CameraUpdate.resolution`; the engine also calls it on \n- `teleport(target: Vector3): void`: Place the camera without smoothing.\n- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3 }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n- `update(u: CameraUpdate): void`\n- `describe(): Record<string, unknown>`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n- `state(): CameraRigState`: The rig as data, exact (`engine.snapshot()`).\n- `setState(s: CameraRigState): void`: Put the rig back where `state()` found it (the same preset).\n\n### class RippleField\n\nThe 2D wave equation on a grid (two height buffers, leapfrog): each cell is pulled toward\nthe average of its neighbours, so a dent spreads out as rings, bounces off the edges and\ndies away. Stable for speed × dt / cell < 0.7; `step` substeps when it has to.\n\n- `new RippleField(o: RippleOptions)`\n- `readonly cols: number`\n- `readonly rows: number`\n- `readonly width: number`\n- `readonly depth: number`\n- `readonly cx: number`\n- `readonly cz: number`\n- `speed: number`\n- `damping: number`\n### WAVES_CALM\n\n```ts\nconst WAVES_CALM: readonly Wave[]\n```\n\nA pond on a still day.\n### skyAt()\n\n```ts\nfunction skyAt(hour: number): SkyState\n```\n\nThe sky at `hour` (wraps around 24).\n\n2670:### interface BurstOptions\n2671-\n2672-- `count?: number`: Override the particle count.\n2673-- `direction?: Vec3`: Override the launch direction (e.g. opposite to a skid).\n2674-- `speed?: number`: Multiply launch speed.\n2675-- `scale?: number`: Multiply size.\n2676-- `colors?: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Override the colors for this burst.\n2677-\n2678-### class ParticlePool\n5013:### interface TweenOptions\n5014-\n5015-- `duration?: number`: Seconds (game time). Default 0.3.\n5016-- `delay?: number`: Seconds before it starts.\n5017-- `ease?: Ease`\n5018-- `repeat?: number`: Extra plays after the first (Infinity loops). With `yoyo`, each way counts as one.\n5019-- `yoyo?: boolean`: Play back the other way on every repeat.\n5020-- `onUpdate?: (progress: number) => void`\n5021-- `onComplete?: () => void`\n4167:### type Ease\n4168-\n4169-```ts\n4170:type Ease = EaseName | ((u: number) => number)\n4171-```\n4172-\n4173-### EASE_NAMES\n4174-\n1159:### class ContactShadow\n1160-\n1161-Classic hard-edged blob shadow that sits on the ground under a character.\n1162-Drawn as a TSL disc (step on distance from center) so it quantizes into a crisp\n1163-pixel ellipse in pixel mode. Position it with `place()` each frame.\n1164-\n1165-- `new ContactShadow(radius = 0.45)`\n1166-- `readonly radius: number`\n1167-- `place(x: number, groundY: number, z: number, height: number): void`\n1168-\n4936:### interface TrailOptions\n4937-\n4938-- `points?: number`: Most points kept. Default 24.\n4939-- `width?: number`: Width at the head (m).\n4940-- `life?: number`: Seconds a point lasts. Default 0.35.\n4941-- `color?: number`: Head and tail colours (hex).\n4942-- `tail?: number`\n4943-- `minStep?: number`: A new point only after moving this far (m). Default 0.05.\n4944-\n2884:### buildModel()\n2885-\n2886-```ts\n2887-function buildModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ModelBuild\n2888-```\n2889-\n2890-### class Catalog\n2891-\n2892-- `new Catalog(defs: readonly T[] = [], kind = 'def', tool = '')`\n2893-- `add(...defs: readonly T[]): this`: Add defs; an id that is already taken throws.\n2894-- `has(id: string): boolean`\n2895-- `get(id: string): T`\n2896-- `all(): T[]`\n--\n3094:### interface ModelBuild\n3095-\n3096-- `readonly id: string`\n3097-- `readonly object: Group`: Named after the model; pivots are named Groups inside it.\n3098-- `readonly bounds: Bounds`\n3099-- `readonly anchors: Readonly<Record<string, { readonly at: Vec3; readonly rot: Vec3 }>>`\n3100-- `readonly colliders: readonly ColliderData[]`\n3101-- `readonly light: ModelLightRequest | null`\n17:11. Models and textures (ASSETS.md): `addModelColliders`, `around`, `assetProgress`, `AssetReader`, `BakedTexture`, `bakeTexture`, `boxFrame`, `buildModel`, `Catalog`, `CatalogEntry`, `checkModel`,\n2822:### addModelColliders()","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"164bf0d8-dcb1-419f-9cac-e03173ffb370","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:25:36.804Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### interface PlayerSettings\n\nThe player's settings: the standard picture and engine options every game gets, as plain data\n(sound is the AudioManager's, which keeps its own volumes). A field left out is the game's own\nchoice; a field set is the player's and wins over it. `engine.settings` holds them, applies\nthem, saves them per game and shows them in the settings panel (the ⚙ button).\n\n- `look?: string`: A LOOK_PRESETS name. Left out: the look the game gives each level.\n- `pixelArt?: boolean`: Pixel art (the pixel pass), or false for smooth 3D (render mode `raw`).\n- `pixelSize?: 'fine' | 'chunky'`: The art resolution: `fine` (the game's, 480×270 by default) or `chunky` (two thirds of it: bigger pixels).\n- `quality?: QualityOption`: Shadow and light quality: a level, or `auto` (the device's).\n- `fps?: number`: Frame cap: 60, 30, or 0 for the display's own rate.\n- `debugInfo?: boolean`: The debug panel: frame rate, camera, GPU errors and the game's status.\n\n### class Settings\n\n`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\nsets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\nsaved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\nsettings panel.\n\n- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n- `readonly key: string | null`\n- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n- `get isOpen: boolean`\n- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n- `open(): void`\n- `close(): void`\n- `toggle(): void`\n\n### PIXEL_SIZES\n\n```ts\nconst PIXEL_SIZES: readonly [\"fine\", \"chunky\"]\n```\n\n### interface CameraConfig\n\n- `preset?: CameraPreset`\n- `zoom?: number`: Zoom factor, 1 = preset default, >1 = closer. Ignored by `first`.\n- `minZoom?: number`\n- `maxZoom?: number`\n- `viewHeight?: number`: Ortho presets: visible world height at zoom 1.\n- `pitch?: number`: iso: degrees below horizon / around Y.\n- `yaw?: number`\n- `fov?: number`: Perspective presets: vertical field of view in degrees.\n- `distance?: number`: third: orbit distance at zoom 1.\n- `position?: [number, number, number]`: fixed: camera position and look-at target.\n- `target?: [number, number, number]`\n- `projection?: 'perspective' | 'ortho'`: fixed/free: projection.\n- `stiffness?: number`: Follow smoothing; higher is snappier.\n\n### type CameraPreset\n### class CameraRig\n\nBase rig: owns the three.js camera, zoom and the ground-plane movement basis.\n\n- `new CameraRig(config: CameraConfig)`\n- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera | PerspectiveCamera`\n- `readonly focus: Vector3`: World point the rig is centred on (used for shadow framing).\n- `zoom: number`\n- `readonly minZoom: number`\n- `readonly maxZoom: number`\n- `readonly zoomable: boolean`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n- `readonly hidesTarget: boolean`: First person hides the player model.\n- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n- `controlsCharacter: boolean`: False while the free camera is flying (input drives the camera, not the player).\n- `snap: boolean`: Pixel-snap the camera (ortho only).\n- `aspect: number`: Viewport aspect (width / height), following the art resolution (see `setAspect`).\n- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts\n- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n- `setAspect(aspect: number): void`: Match the art resolution's aspect (adaptive framing changes it with the screen). `update()` calls this from `CameraUpdate.resolution`; the engine also calls it on \n- `teleport(target: Vector3): void`: Place the camera without smoothing.\n- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3 }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n- `update(u: CameraUpdate): void`\n- `describe(): Record<string, unknown>`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n- `state(): CameraRigState`: The rig as data, exact (`engine.snapshot()`).\n- `setState(s: CameraRigState): void`: Put the rig back where `state()` found it (the same preset).\n\n### class RippleField\n\nThe 2D wave equation on a grid (two height buffers, leapfrog): each cell is pulled toward\nthe average of its neighbours, so a dent spreads out as rings, bounces off the edges and\ndies away. Stable for speed × dt / cell < 0.7; `step` substeps when it has to.\n\n- `new RippleField(o: RippleOptions)`\n- `readonly cols: number`\n- `readonly rows: number`\n- `readonly width: number`\n- `readonly depth: number`\n- `readonly cx: number`\n- `readonly cz: number`\n- `speed: number`\n- `damping: number`\n### WAVES_CALM\n\n```ts\nconst WAVES_CALM: readonly Wave[]\n```\n\nA pond on a still day.\n### skyAt()\n\n```ts\nfunction skyAt(hour: number): SkyState\n```\n\nThe sky at `hour` (wraps around 24).\n\n2670:### interface BurstOptions\n2671-\n2672-- `count?: number`: Override the particle count.\n2673-- `direction?: Vec3`: Override the launch direction (e.g. opposite to a skid).\n2674-- `speed?: number`: Multiply launch speed.\n2675-- `scale?: number`: Multiply size.\n2676-- `colors?: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Override the colors for this burst.\n2677-\n2678-### class ParticlePool\n5013:### interface TweenOptions\n5014-\n5015-- `duration?: number`: Seconds (game time). Default 0.3.\n5016-- `delay?: number`: Seconds before it starts.\n5017-- `ease?: Ease`\n5018-- `repeat?: number`: Extra plays after the first (Infinity loops). With `yoyo`, each way counts as one.\n5019-- `yoyo?: boolean`: Play back the other way on every repeat.\n5020-- `onUpdate?: (progress: number) => void`\n5021-- `onComplete?: () => void`\n4167:### type Ease\n4168-\n4169-```ts\n4170:type Ease = EaseName | ((u: number) => number)\n4171-```\n4172-\n4173-### EASE_NAMES\n4174-\n1159:### class ContactShadow\n1160-\n1161-Classic hard-edged blob shadow that sits on the ground under a character.\n1162-Drawn as a TSL disc (step on distance from center) so it quantizes into a crisp\n1163-pixel ellipse in pixel mode. Position it with `place()` each frame.\n1164-\n1165-- `new ContactShadow(radius = 0.45)`\n1166-- `readonly radius: number`\n1167-- `place(x: number, groundY: number, z: number, height: number): void`\n1168-\n4936:### interface TrailOptions\n4937-\n4938-- `points?: number`: Most points kept. Default 24.\n4939-- `width?: number`: Width at the head (m).\n4940-- `life?: number`: Seconds a point lasts. Default 0.35.\n4941-- `color?: number`: Head and tail colours (hex).\n4942-- `tail?: number`\n4943-- `minStep?: number`: A new point only after moving this far (m). Default 0.05.\n4944-\n2884:### buildModel()\n2885-\n2886-```ts\n2887-function buildModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ModelBuild\n2888-```\n2889-\n2890-### class Catalog\n2891-\n2892-- `new Catalog(defs: readonly T[] = [], kind = 'def', tool = '')`\n2893-- `add(...defs: readonly T[]): this`: Add defs; an id that is already taken throws.\n2894-- `has(id: string): boolean`\n2895-- `get(id: string): T`\n2896-- `all(): T[]`\n--\n3094:### interface ModelBuild\n3095-\n3096-- `readonly id: string`\n3097-- `readonly object: Group`: Named after the model; pivots are named Groups inside it.\n3098-- `readonly bounds: Bounds`\n3099-- `readonly anchors: Readonly<Record<string, { readonly at: Vec3; readonly rot: Vec3 }>>`\n3100-- `readonly colliders: readonly ColliderData[]`\n3101-- `readonly light: ModelLightRequest | null`\n17:11. Models and textures (ASSETS.md): `addModelColliders`, `around`, `assetProgress`, `AssetReader`, `BakedTexture`, `bakeTexture`, `boxFrame`, `buildModel`, `Catalog`, `CatalogEntry`, `checkModel`,\n2822:### addModelColliders()","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SSqDWx7YtZagyWVh44jh8P","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
