{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjP69VRgAZQfJw1WSZ26","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Sph2K3e5Q7DAbkPGyAzz1K","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/WeFitIn-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-230741\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/data/about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  answers: ['unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'],\n};\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK\"\"\",\"\"\"  answers: [\n    'About 50. Scripts caught about 20 (a crash, a dead activity, ghost messages that never reached other players, a save field lost on reload, and balance). Screenshots caught about 30 that scripts could not see (avatars vanishing, a dial hiding Ounce, labels over heads).',\n    'Five. Step Class avatars vanished from a bad ease name. Avatars folded into heaps from a lean that added up every frame. Vitamin Tray scored 0 for everyone because resting bodies slept through gravity changes. Step Class crashed on a mat colour. Online, ghosts never received their messages.',\n    'Running five bot skills through every activity. In one command it found a crash and a dead activity, and it gave every balance number I tuned against. The 1920x1080 contact sheets were the close second.',\n    'The WebKit and Firefox runs. Neither has WebGPU on this machine, so they only prove that the failure message shows.',\n  ],\n};\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  answers: ['unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'none', 'unknown'],\n};\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK\"\"\",\"\"\"  answers: [\n    'Headless in Node. The same game code, physics and mixers ran a full seven-day playthrough with bots in about a minute, so I could test the real game constantly. Models as data with checkModel came second.',\n    'Yes. A ClipDef key takes its own ease names (in, out), not the tween names, and outQuad baked NaN with validateClip and analyzeClip both silent: avatars vanished only when the clip played. I also hung a script awaiting a scene change in manual time, and lost Tray to Rapier bodies sleeping through a gravity change.',\n    'The Dot and its driver seam: one lean model that a person, a pad, a bot or a ghost can all drive, used by every activity, attract, the tests and online. Close behind, the HUD kit: mixed-case text, discs, rings, menus and prompts.',\n    'The HUD is only rects, text and sprites, with no circles or alpha. Dials are drawn as scanlines, and menu dimming borrows the transition uniform. Also, pads are merged into one, so Family Hour reads navigator.getGamepads itself.',\n    'none',\n    'Make validateClip reject an unknown ease name. It would have saved the worst bug of the run, and it is a small change.',\n  ],\n};\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"export const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = {\n  questions: ['What did you like most about this prompt?', 'What was confusing?', 'What was the hardest thing to do?', 'What would you change in this prompt?'],\n  answers: ['unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'],\n};\"\"\",\"\"\"export const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = {\n  questions: ['What did you like most about this prompt?', 'What was confusing?', 'What was the hardest thing to do?', 'What would you change in this prompt?'],\n  answers: [\n    'The verified recipes in the plan. Knowing which numbers and calls were already proven meant I could spend the effort on the game, and the bot table let me check the core feel at once.',\n    'Coconut Header is listed for lane staging with classmates on side mats, but also gets a wider lane when solo; I made solo one wide lane. Bias values such as +.10 have no stated unit; I treated them as stick lean, multiplied by authority.',\n    'Keeping every screen readable at 480x270 with pad, keys and mouse all working, while a dozen activities share one HUD. Composition took several rounds of screenshots.',\n    'Say whether Header solo has classmates, and give the unit for bias. Ask for contact sheets of every screen as a step, since they caught more than I expected.',\n  ],\n};\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/headless/core.mjs'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"import { AI_HUB, CREDITS, SOURCE_INFO, exitInterview } from '../../src/data/about.js';\",\"import { AI_HUB, CREDITS, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, PROMPT_FEEDBACK, SOURCE_INFO, TESTING_FEEDBACK, exitInterview } from '../../src/data/about.js';\")\ns=s.replace(\"...Object.values(SOURCE_INFO), ...CREDITS, TITLE];\",\"...Object.values(SOURCE_INFO), ...CREDITS, TITLE, ...[TESTING_FEEDBACK, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, PROMPT_FEEDBACK].flatMap((b) => [...b.questions, ...b.answers])];\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  eq(AI_HUB.name, TITLE);\n});\"\"\",\"\"\"  eq(AI_HUB.name, TITLE);\n  for (const list of [e.testingFeedback, e.engineFeedback, e.promptFeedback]) for (const a of list) assert(a !== 'unknown' && a.length > 3, 'every feedback answer is filled in');\n});\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 -c \"print('ok')\"; tail -2 .scratch/full-test.log 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-200","description":"Fill in the testing, engine and prompt feedback answers","timeout":20000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3336,"cache_read_input_tokens":698797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3336},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"d84467b4-079c-4507-a827-478a85df9831","timestamp":"2026-11-05T07:24:51.099Z","request_id":"req_011CgjP694dxKgo4TPyhsepv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Sph2K3e5Q7DAbkPGyAzz1K":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/WeFitIn-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-230741\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/data/about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  answers: ['unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'],\n};\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK\"\"\",\"\"\"  answers: [\n    'About 50. Scripts caught about 20 (a crash, a dead activity, ghost messages that never reached other players, a save field lost on reload, and balance). Screenshots caught about 30 that scripts could not see (avatars vanishing, a dial hiding Ounce, labels over heads).',\n    'Five. Step Class avatars vanished from a bad ease name. Avatars folded into heaps from a lean that added up every frame. Vitamin Tray scored 0 for everyone because resting bodies slept through gravity changes. Step Class crashed on a mat colour. Online, ghosts never received their messages.',\n    'Running five bot skills through every activity. In one command it found a crash and a dead activity, and it gave every balance number I tuned against. The 1920x1080 contact sheets were the close second.',\n    'The WebKit and Firefox runs. Neither has WebGPU on this machine, so they only prove that the failure message shows.',\n  ],\n};\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  answers: ['unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'none', 'unknown'],\n};\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK\"\"\",\"\"\"  answers: [\n    'Headless in Node. The same game code, physics and mixers ran a full seven-day playthrough with bots in about a minute, so I could test the real game constantly. Models as data with checkModel came second.',\n    'Yes. A ClipDef key takes its own ease names (in, out), not the tween names, and outQuad baked NaN with validateClip and analyzeClip both silent: avatars vanished only when the clip played. I also hung a script awaiting a scene change in manual time, and lost Tray to Rapier bodies sleeping through a gravity change.',\n    'The Dot and its driver seam: one lean model that a person, a pad, a bot or a ghost can all drive, used by every activity, attract, the tests and online. Close behind, the HUD kit: mixed-case text, discs, rings, menus and prompts.',\n    'The HUD is only rects, text and sprites, with no circles or alpha. Dials are drawn as scanlines, and menu dimming borrows the transition uniform. Also, pads are merged into one, so Family Hour reads navigator.getGamepads itself.',\n    'none',\n    'Make validateClip reject an unknown ease name. It would have saved the worst bug of the run, and it is a small change.',\n  ],\n};\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"export const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = {\n  questions: ['What did you like most about this prompt?', 'What was confusing?', 'What was the hardest thing to do?', 'What would you change in this prompt?'],\n  answers: ['unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown', 'unknown'],\n};\"\"\",\"\"\"export const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = {\n  questions: ['What did you like most about this prompt?', 'What was confusing?', 'What was the hardest thing to do?', 'What would you change in this prompt?'],\n  answers: [\n    'The verified recipes in the plan. Knowing which numbers and calls were already proven meant I could spend the effort on the game, and the bot table let me check the core feel at once.',\n    'Coconut Header is listed for lane staging with classmates on side mats, but also gets a wider lane when solo; I made solo one wide lane. Bias values such as +.10 have no stated unit; I treated them as stick lean, multiplied by authority.',\n    'Keeping every screen readable at 480x270 with pad, keys and mouse all working, while a dozen activities share one HUD. Composition took several rounds of screenshots.',\n    'Say whether Header solo has classmates, and give the unit for bias. Ask for contact sheets of every screen as a step, since they caught more than I expected.',\n  ],\n};\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/headless/core.mjs'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"import { AI_HUB, CREDITS, SOURCE_INFO, exitInterview } from '../../src/data/about.js';\",\"import { AI_HUB, CREDITS, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, PROMPT_FEEDBACK, SOURCE_INFO, TESTING_FEEDBACK, exitInterview } from '../../src/data/about.js';\")\ns=s.replace(\"...Object.values(SOURCE_INFO), ...CREDITS, TITLE];\",\"...Object.values(SOURCE_INFO), ...CREDITS, TITLE, ...[TESTING_FEEDBACK, ENGINE_FEEDBACK, PROMPT_FEEDBACK].flatMap((b) => [...b.questions, ...b.answers])];\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  eq(AI_HUB.name, TITLE);\n});\"\"\",\"\"\"  eq(AI_HUB.name, TITLE);\n  for (const list of [e.testingFeedback, e.engineFeedback, e.promptFeedback]) for (const a of list) assert(a !== 'unknown' && a.length > 3, 'every feedback answer is filled in');\n});\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 -c \"print('ok')\"; tail -2 .scratch/full-test.log 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-200","description":"Fill in the testing, engine and prompt feedback answers","timeout":20000}}}
