{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjRBAzr9tWPHbwK4woze","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**We Fit In** is finished and in this folder. It's an original fitness comedy where a small, polite bathroom scale runs a wellness island, and your whole body is one dot you keep in a circle. The final build passes all 289 scripted tests, but no person has played it, so balance and feel were only checked with bots and screenshots.\n\n## What's in the game\n- **Story week:** seven days ending in the Long Stand and Ounce's confession, then an open-ended Week 2.\n- **Activities:** 16, plus the finale. All of them are also open from Drop-In Class, with hard versions.\n- **Multiplayer:** the Medley runs as Family Hour on one screen (1–4 players) and as AI Hub ghost mode online.\n- **Everything else in the plan:** attract mode, Dev Tools with live sliders, Settings, Locker Room, Hall of Numbers, Sweat Jar, code-written music and gibberish voices (music at 10% by default), and the touch-only message.\n\n## How it was checked\n- **Scripted tests:** a full playthrough from a fresh save through Week 1 into Week 2, using the real menus with bots playing the activities. The rest cover input, saves, attract and audio levels.\n- **AI Hub:** all four harness runs pass, including host-leave with latency and packet loss.\n- **Stand-ins only:** a stub gamepad, a phone profile on desktop Chromium, and measured audio levels, with no real controller, phone or listening.\n- **Screens:** I looked at them at 1920×1080. Layout overflow was checked by script at four window sizes.\n- **WebGPU only:** on this machine Firefox and WebKit can only show the \"WebGPU unavailable\" message.\n\n## Where I departed from the plan\n- **Coconut Header:** solo is one wide lane with no classmates, because the plan says both.\n- **Vitamin Tray:** pills release 3 at a time, because all 8 at once wasn't really playable.\n- **Island Jog:** the path is about 200 m, not 220 m.\n- **Source files:** a few are merged, such as the session card living in `medley.js`.\n\nTo re-run the tests, run `npm install` then `node tools/test.mjs`; I removed `node_modules` when cleaning up. Nothing is committed to git.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 23:07:41\n- **Source:** Wii Fit\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** fitness and balance minigame collection inside a light life-sim week (sports). Isometric on the island, fixed front-on for class activities, other fixed views per activity (behind, side-on, top-down-ish).\n- **Tech:** Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (riftlight engine kit) with three.js r186 and Rapier as bundled in it; esbuild 0.28.2 for packaging; vanilla JavaScript modules\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native pixel look (toon materials, 16-colour palette), with new models written as data for a spotless white island made of giant gym equipment\n- **Animation:** engine ClipDefs with THREE.AnimationMixer, plus scrubbed reps, Squash, SpringChain and additive lean layers\n- **Audio:** engine Song and SoundDef data plus a Web Audio formant voice, all code with no files. Gibberish voices per speaker. Music 10% by default.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1–4 players; Family Hour is local on one screen\n- **Testing:** headless Node playthroughs with bots behind one test command; Chromium, Firefox and WebKit with Playwright on file://; gamepad stub, phone profile, OfflineAudioContext and AnalyserNode checks; the hub harness; screenshots at 1920×1080 only for what a script can't judge; no subagents for review\n- **Research:** read the kit guides and the hub README, searched API.md. The director's plan included engine and hub research and spikes.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\n- **Usage:** added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 50. Scripts caught about 20 (a crash, a dead activity, ghost messages that never reached other players, a save field lost on reload, and balance). Screenshots caught about 30 that scripts could not see (avatars vanishing, a dial hiding Ounce, labels over heads).\n2. **How many were critical or game breaking?** Five. Step Class avatars vanished from a bad ease name. Avatars folded into heaps from a lean that added up every frame. Vitamin Tray scored 0 for everyone because resting bodies slept through gravity changes. Step Class crashed on a mat colour. Online, ghosts never received their messages.\n3. **Most helpful test?** Running five bot skills through every activity. In one command it found a crash and a dead activity, and it gave every balance number I tuned against. The 1920×1080 contact sheets were a close second.\n4. **Least helpful test?** The WebKit and Firefox runs. Neither has WebGPU on this machine, so they only prove that the failure message shows.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most?** Headless in Node. The same game code, physics and mixers ran a full seven-day playthrough with bots in about a minute, so I could test the real game constantly. Models as data with `checkModel` came second.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. A ClipDef key takes its own ease names (`in`, `out`), not the tween names, and `outQuad` baked NaN with `validateClip` and `analyzeClip` both silent, so avatars vanished only when the clip played. I also hung a script awaiting a scene change in manual time, and lost Tray to Rapier bodies sleeping through a gravity change.\n3. **Most important thing you had to build?** The Dot and its driver seam: one lean model that a person, a pad, a bot or a ghost can all drive, used by every activity, attract, the tests and online. Close behind is the HUD kit: mixed-case text, discs, rings, menus and prompts.\n4. **Hardest part?** The HUD is only rects, text and sprites, with no circles or alpha. Dials are drawn as scanlines, and menu dimming borrows the transition uniform. Pads are also merged into one, so Family Hour reads `navigator.getGamepads` itself.\n5. **What did you change in the engine?** None.\n6. **One thing to change?** Make `validateClip` reject an unknown ease name. It would have saved the worst bug of the run, and it's a small change.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most?** The verified recipes in the plan. Knowing which numbers and calls were already proven meant I could spend the effort on the game, and the bot table let me check the core feel at once.\n2. **What was confusing?** Coconut Header is listed for lane staging with classmates on side mats, but also gets a wider lane when solo; I made solo one wide lane. Bias values such as +.10 have no stated unit; I treated them as stick lean, multiplied by authority.\n3. **Hardest thing to do?** Keeping every screen readable at 480×270 with pad, keys and mouse all working, while a dozen activities share one HUD. Composition took several rounds of screenshots.\n4. **What would you change?** Say whether Header solo has classmates, and give the unit for bias. Ask for contact sheets of every screen as a step, since they caught more than I expected.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `WeFitIn-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-230741.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `WeFitIn-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-230741/` (dev folder)\n- `PROGRESS.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":520,"cache_read_input_tokens":724839,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":520},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"21525021-50cf-415a-b456-14a5c7e30adf","timestamp":"2026-11-05T07:52:18.806Z","request_id":"req_011CgjRBAa3AZieZj6D676Lc"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.]: Not satisfied. The transcript shows the deliverables exist (single html and exit-interview.json in root, dev folder with the engine). But PLAN.md's sections 3-9 call for many things the transcript doesn't show were done: PLAN 19 build order step 3 demands stopping to judge Holding Still's feel, and the agent asked for capture-based checks in several places. More importantly, PLAN 21 requires each item in the brief checklist to be ticked, the Done section requires 'No TODOs, placeholders, or stubs' (the agent left 'void' placeholders and an 'unknown' Testing Feedback answer was replaced, but the Source Information plan field and several PLAN items such as Research spikes and the 120+ line count rely on partial evidence), and the agent openly acknowledged untested items: no real controller, phone, or listening test, and only 2 of the 4 browser engines were exercised. PLAN 9 requires the About screen to hold the feedback; the transcript shows it was written but the CREDITS.md page and the in-game screens were only partly verified. Since the plan says that anything doable on this computer must be done, and the transcript shows partial verification rather than a full completion check against PLAN 21, the condition cannot be confirmed from transcript evidence alone."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"92c49415-ff2e-4102-b6d7-76035273af89","timestamp":"2026-11-05T07:52:26.306Z","isSynthetic":true}
