{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjUbo819umFYqFhwzYCp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hook has a point again, and this time it isn't only about evidence. It says I captured static poses rather than a real run. That made me ask what else the bots have been hiding, and I see a much bigger gap: **the bots bypass the input layer**. Nothing has proved that each activity is actually playable with keys, pad or mouse, and Step's real audio clock has never run, because autopilot switches it off.\n\nA closer re-read of the plan also shows requirements I missed: the 12 px safe margin, 2 px minimum lines, teal speaker names, dusk lanterns, and some tuning values that aren't in `src/data`.\n\nI'll do all of it, starting with device-level play, since that could reveal real problems."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3793,"cache_read_input_tokens":846968,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3793},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"77dea90e-2e2f-4f05-97e5-d45902fd6c8e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T08:38:17.695Z","request_id":"req_011CgjUbngTcSbN5s5CUoiMh"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjUbo819umFYqFhwzYCp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018Nu7qYw6iw3T8VgMWh93iv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/WeFitIn-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-230741\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='../PROGRESS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns+=\"\"\"\n## Second audit (stop hook again): work list\nBots bypass input, so: device-level play of every activity with keys, pad, mouse (tests/headless/play.mjs); real-time Step audio clock in a browser; real captured Holding Still run with body-vs-Dot correlation; keyboard and mouse rows of the bot table; CREDITS.md scrolled to its end with exact text; WebKit/Firefox failure screens and AIHub.fail; hub mouse and pad tests; hammock branches; classmate reaction; Long Stand schedule; rep gag; step windows; no Math.random. Plan misses: 12 px safe margin (strict layout test), 2 px lines, teal speaker names, dusk lanterns, HEADER/PIER into src/data, no pause after session end, Research field wording.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n(timeout 110 npm install --no-audit --no-fund --silent </dev/null 2>&1 | tail -1); node -p \"require('./node_modules/playwright/package.json').version\" </dev/null; mkdir -p .scratch\ncat > tests/headless/_people.mjs <<'EOF'\n// People, as far as a script can be one: they see late, press real keys, hold a real stick, move a real mouse.\n// Nothing here touches autopilot or an activity's botInput: only the input layer, as a player's hands do.\nimport { App } from '../lib.mjs';\n\nconst PAD_KEYS = { up: 'KeyW', down: 'KeyS', left: 'KeyA', right: 'KeyD' };\n\n/** The three devices, behind one small interface: lean(x, y) and press / hold by role. */\nexport function makeHands(engine, device) {\n  const input = engine.input;\n  const held = new Set();\n  const setHeld = (code, on) => { if (on && !held.has(code)) { input.setKey(code, true); held.add(code); } else if (!on && held.has(code)) { input.setKey(code, false); held.delete(code); } };\n  let tapQueue = [];\n  const tap = (code) => { input.setKey(code, true); tapQueue.push(code); };\n  const release = () => { for (const c of tapQueue) input.setKey(c, false); tapQueue = []; };\n  const ROLES = {\n    keyboard: { stepL: 'KeyF', stepR: 'KeyJ', confirm: 'Space', breath: 'Space' },\n    pad: { stepL: 'PadL1', stepR: 'PadR1', confirm: 'PadCross', breath: 'PadR2' },\n    mouse: { stepL: 'MouseLeft', stepR: 'MouseRight', confirm: 'MouseLeft', breath: 'MouseLeft' },\n  }[device];\n  const hands = {\n    device,\n    /** Lean toward (x, y), each -1..1. Keys can only be on or off: Shift gives half. */\n    lean(x, y, dial) {\n      if (device === 'keyboard') {\n        const mag = Math.hypot(x, y);\n        setHeld('ShiftLeft', mag > 0.12 && mag < 0.55);\n        setHeld(PAD_KEYS.right, x > 0.12); setHeld(PAD_KEYS.left, x < -0.12);\n        setHeld(PAD_KEYS.up, y > 0.12); setHeld(PAD_KEYS.down, y < -0.12);\n      } else if (device === 'pad') {\n        hands.stick.x = x; hands.stick.y = y;\n      } else {\n        const hud = engine.hud;\n        const r = App.T.mouseLeanRadius;\n        const c = dial ?? { x: hud.width / 2, y: hud.height / 2 };\n        const ax = c.x + x * r, ay = c.y - y * r;\n        input.setPointer((ax / hud.width) * 2 - 1, 1 - (ay / hud.height) * 2, false);\n      }\n    },\n    stick: { x: 0, y: 0 },\n    hold(role, on) {\n      if (device === 'mouse' && ROLES[role] === 'MouseLeft') { input.setButtons(on ? 1 : 0); return; }\n      setHeld(ROLES[role], on);\n    },\n    press(role) {\n      if (device === 'mouse') { input.setButtons(role === 'stepR' ? 2 : 1); tapQueue.push('__mouse'); return; }\n      tap(ROLES[role]);\n    },\n    endFrame() {\n      if (tapQueue.includes('__mouse')) input.setButtons(0);\n      tapQueue = tapQueue.filter((c) => c !== '__mouse');\n      release();\n    },\n    letGo() { for (const c of [...held]) setHeld(c, false); hands.stick.x = 0; hands.stick.y = 0; if (device === 'mouse') input.setButtons(0); },\n    /** Say which device this person is using, the way the game would notice. */\n    announce() {\n      if (device === 'mouse') { input.setPointer(0.01, 0.01, false); engine.step(1); input.setPointer(0, 0, false); engine.step(1); App.device.last = 'mouse'; App.device.lastDesk = 'mouse'; }\n      if (device === 'pad') App.device.last = 'pad';\n      if (device === 'keyboard') { App.device.last = 'keyboard'; App.device.lastDesk = 'keyboard'; }\n    },\n  };\n  return hands;\n}\n\n/** Sees the Dot late, overshoots a bit, gets better with skill: the plan's human-like controller. */\nexport class Eyes {\n  constructor({ tau = 0.22, kp = 1.5, kd = 0.55 } = {}) { this.n = Math.round(tau * 60); this.kp = kp; this.kd = kd; this.h = []; }\n  /** Call once a frame. Returns the lean to apply toward a target. */\n  lean(dot, tx = 0, ty = 0) {\n    this.h.push([dot.x, dot.y, dot.vx, dot.vy]);\n    if (this.h.length > this.n + 1) this.h.shift();\n    const [x, y, vx, vy] = this.h[0];\n    let ux = -this.kp * (x - tx) - this.kd * vx, uy = -this.kp * (y - ty) - this.kd * vy;\n    const d = Math.hypot(ux, uy);\n    if (d > 1) { ux /= d; uy /= d; }\n    return [ux, uy];\n  }\n}\nEOF\ncat > .scratch/padprobe.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport { boot, App } from '../tests/lib.mjs';\nconst pad = { id:'Stub', index:0, connected:true, mapping:'standard', timestamp:0, axes:[0,0,0,0], buttons:Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,value:0,touched:false})) };\nObject.defineProperty(globalThis.navigator,'getGamepads',{value:()=>[pad,null,null,null],configurable:true});\nconst h = await boot({ scene:'title' });\nh.step(2); console.log('axis idle',App.engine.input.padAxis, 'connected',App.engine.input.gamepadConnected);\npad.axes[0]=.8; pad.axes[1]=-.6; h.step(3); console.log('axis pushed',App.engine.input.padAxis, App.engine.input.moveAxis());\npad.buttons[0].pressed=true; h.step(2); pad.buttons[0].pressed=false; h.step(2); console.log('stack',App.state().stack,'device',App.device.last);\nprocess.exit(0);\nEOF\ntimeout 60 node .scratch/padprobe.mjs </dev/null 2>&1 | tail -4 | cut -c1-200","description":"Reinstall Playwright, write human-like input helpers, probe the pad path in Node","timeout":190000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3793,"cache_read_input_tokens":846968,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3793},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"ad3c2ce8-fce4-4bdb-a24f-dd82e64d4d4d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T08:38:41.273Z","request_id":"req_011CgjUbngTcSbN5s5CUoiMh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018Nu7qYw6iw3T8VgMWh93iv":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/WeFitIn-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-230741\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='../PROGRESS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns+=\"\"\"\n## Second audit (stop hook again): work list\nBots bypass input, so: device-level play of every activity with keys, pad, mouse (tests/headless/play.mjs); real-time Step audio clock in a browser; real captured Holding Still run with body-vs-Dot correlation; keyboard and mouse rows of the bot table; CREDITS.md scrolled to its end with exact text; WebKit/Firefox failure screens and AIHub.fail; hub mouse and pad tests; hammock branches; classmate reaction; Long Stand schedule; rep gag; step windows; no Math.random. Plan misses: 12 px safe margin (strict layout test), 2 px lines, teal speaker names, dusk lanterns, HEADER/PIER into src/data, no pause after session end, Research field wording.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\n