a real mouse. Bots skip the input layer, so only these could find that a mouse could not jump at Pier Jump. Next came the bot sweep, which found a crash and gave every balance number, and the 1920x1080 contact sheets.',\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"    'Say whether Header solo has classmates, and give the unit for bias. Ask for contact sheets of every screen as a step, since they caught more than I expected.',\"\"\",\"\"\"    'Say whether Header solo has classmates, and give the unit for bias. Ask for contact sheets of every screen as a step, and say that tests must play through the real input as well as with bots, since those two caught more than I expected.',\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"  testing: 'Headless Node playthroughs with bots, one test command;\"\"\",\"\"\"  testing: 'Headless Node playthroughs with bots, plus scripts playing through real keys, stick and mouse, one test command;\"\"\"),\n])\np='../PROGRESS.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns+=\"\"\"\nSecond audit results so far: play.mjs (keys, pad, mouse through the real input layer) found Pier Jump could not be jumped with a mouse. details.mjs found click-to-walk hitting invisible walls, hoops dropping during the count, Step matching stale notes. Strict 12 px margin applied everywhere (layout test now enforces it). Firefox with prefs forced: navigator.gpu present, adapter null; WebKit: no navigator.gpu: neither can run the game here, failure screens looked at, AIHub.fail voids the round. Real Holding Still run captured as 12 frames and looked at; head/Dot correlation test added. CREDITS.md compared character for character and scrolled to its last line.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"^import.*layout\" tests/headless/systems.mjs | cut -c1-80; echo patched","description":"Hold the Podium menu until Ounce finishes and update the feedback answers","timeout":20000}}}
