{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, TaskStop, ToolSearch</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - The user ran `/goal`: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\" A session Stop hook enforces this and has twice replied \"Not satisfied\".\n   - STAGE.md: \"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\"\n   - TASK.md deliverables:\n     - Single html `WeFitIn-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-230741.html` in root.\n     - `exit-interview.json` in root (exact shape, parses as JSON).\n     - Dev subfolder of the same base name.\n     - Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in BOTH the final chat reply AND the in-game About/Credits screen.\n   - Game: an original fitness comedy inspired by Wii Fit (no Nintendo names, characters, look or music in the game).\n   - Constraints from TASK.md and the system, which remain in force:\n     - \"Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"\n     - \"Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\"\n     - \"The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\" Keep one or two browsers open at once.\n     - \"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\" Tests stay behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count.\n     - Never edit `pixel-engine.js`; keep the hub's `session.js` unmodified.\n     - Commit or push only when the user asks (nothing has been committed).\n     - The user's email is for identification only.\n     - Use they/them for people whose pronouns aren't stated.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (WebGPU only, three.js r186, Rapier bundled); `Engine.start`, `Engine.headless` (Node), `engine.step()` manual time; a Game is a class with `setup/fixedUpdate/update/cameraTarget/status/fingerprint`.\n   - The HUD is only rect, text and sprite, in art pixels (480×270, `aspect:'fill'`). Models and clips are data (`model()`, `ClipDef`, `compileClips`, `checkModel`, `validateClip`, `analyzeClip`, `renderSheet`). Clip eases are `linear|in|out|inOut|hold|inBack|outBack`, NOT tween names.\n   - AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card; harness `window.__hubCheck.pass`.\n   - The Dot: an unstable weight (`src/core/dot.js`) with drivers (Local, Keyboard, Pad, Bot, Ghost); bots are a delayed PD controller.\n   - Testing tips:\n     - Awaiting `App.go` in manual mode hangs unless frames are stepped.\n     - In `tools/shot.mjs` page scripts use `await go(id,args)`, `wait()`, `G` (App), `e` (engine).\n     - Wait on long runs with `timeout 595 tail -f <log> </dev/null | grep -m1 \"^exit\"`.\n     - Use `timeout` and `</dev/null` on node commands. Never run bare `cat`. Foreground `sleep` is blocked.\n     - Browser tests should wait in frames, not milliseconds (shared machine, software rendering).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   Root: `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/` holds PLAN.md, TASK.md, STAGE.md, PROGRESS.md, the html, exit-interview.json and the dev folder `WeFitIn-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-230741/`.\n\n   Dev folder holds kit files untouched (hash in `vendor/pixel-engine.sha256`), `vendor/hub/*`, `package.json` (devDependencies playwright exactly \"1.63.0\") and `.gitignore`.\n   - `src/main.js`, `src/app.js` (App singleton: `go`, `state`, `setDriver`, `continueWeek`, `ringOf`, `layout`, `voiceApi`).\n   - `src/core/`: dot, drivers (`readPresses()` takes MouseLeft once and hands it to both stepL and confirm), actions, device, tunables, save (keeps `dropin`), net, clock, week.\n   - `src/ui/`:\n     - font, widgets (`ring`/`line` clamp to ≥2 px, `panel` thick=2), layout (`PROMPT_Y=23`, `ABOVE_PROMPTS=30`, `overflow(w,h,margin)`), menu (`o.x` is the panel's left edge).\n     - dialogue (Bark `draw(hud,bottom=12)`), prompts, stack (a screen hides those beneath unless `opaque===false`), chart, activity-hud.\n     - `screens/{common,results,pause,settings,howto,about,dev,soundtest,mainmenu}.js`.\n   - `src/audio/{voice,songs,sfx}.js`; `src/art/{avatar,props,models,textures,clips,glyphs,particles,portraits}.js`.\n   - `src/data/{title,activities,poses,reps,charts,boards,week,lines,questions,unlocks,classmates,stations,medley,about,alllines,howto,hoop,slackline,jog,longstand,games,credits-text}.js` (`games.js` holds HEADER and PIER; `credits-text.js` is generated by the build).\n   - `src/scenes/`: base, boot, index, sets, title, attract, hub (`stationAtPointer`, `pointOnRay`; ray goes to the ground plane, past invisible walls), weighin, report, jar, records, locker, ferry, ending (Timeline), viewer, medley, card, join; `activity/{base,lanes,events,poses,reps,hoop,step,header,slackline,tray,pier,jog,longstand}.js`.\n   - `tools/`: `build.mjs` (html + exit-interview, parses JSON), `test.mjs` (`--fast`, name filters), `shot.mjs`, `clip-sheet.mjs`.\n   - `tests/`:\n     - `lib.mjs`, `lib-pure.mjs`.\n     - `headless/{core,activities,week,systems,layout,play,details}.mjs`, `headless/_people.mjs` (stub pad, `makeHands`, `Eyes`, `PLAYS`).\n     - `browser/{_lib,game,devices,hub}.mjs`.\n\n   Latest edit (`tests/browser/game.mjs`): `assert(r.pressed >= 4, ...)` with the comment \"the opening bars are sparse: two notes a bar\".\n\n4. Errors and fixes (main ones):\n   - Bare `cat` hung the shell: avoid it.\n   - `shot.mjs` hung by awaiting `G.go` in manual mode: added a `go()` helper that steps frames.\n   - Lean accumulated on joints with no track: Avatar now restores the pose before `mixer.update`.\n   - `'outQuad'` in ClipDef baked NaN (Step avatars vanished): replaced with `'out'`; added a NaN track test.\n   - Tray bodies slept through gravity changes: `setCanSleep(false)`. Step mat palette crash fixed.\n   - Lane constructor dropped `seat`, so ghosts got no messages: fixed. Medley idled 10 s at the end: fixed.\n   - Esc in Jar/Hall opened pause: `canPause=false` there. Drop-In records weren't reloaded: fixed. A Drop-In Long Stand routed to the ending: fixed.\n   - Test runner race lost results: fixed.\n   - `npm install` pulled Playwright 1.64.1 because the pin had silently missed: now exact 1.63.0.\n   - Coach's bark hid prompts: `barkBottom()`. Card ready ticks clipped: moved into name tags. Attract banner clipped on phones: wrapped. Podium bark covered the menu: the menu waits for the bark.\n   - Mouse couldn't jump at Pier (foot check consumed the click): `readPresses`.\n   - Click-to-walk hit invisible walls: ground-plane ray.\n   - Hoops dropped during the countdown: `countStep` only runs for poses.\n   - Step matched stale notes: `err > ok` skipped.\n   - 12 px safe margin, 2 px lines and teal names were missing: fixed and enforced. Strict layout test passes on 4 sizes plus phone.\n   - Test-only fixes: flaky phone wait (now frames); \"unknown\" regex in About test (now exact answer check); scripted keyboard Tray player (holds Shift, rolls cell by cell).\n   - Stray `/tmp/.none` was created and removed.\n\n5. Problem Solving (evidence so far):\n   - `check.mjs --sheets src/art/models.js`: 36 models, 0 problems, 0 warnings. `check.mjs` on the built html: OK on WebGPU, exit 0.\n   - All 34 clip sheets looked at.\n   - Real Holding Still run captured as 12 frames and looked at; head/Dot correlation test added.\n   - All About pages looked at; CREDITS.md compared character by character and scrolled to its last line (details.mjs).\n   - All glyph sets, session card, story beats, Dev Tools, phone view and failure screens looked at.\n   - Firefox with prefs forced: `navigator.gpu` present, adapter null. WebKit: no `navigator.gpu`. So neither can run the game here; the failure message is tested, and in a session the round voids (\"round 1 void: no-players\").\n   - Real-time Step audio clock tested on a timer, independent of frame rate.\n   - Bot table through the real scene: pad 78/58/39/21, keyboard 78/58/40/24, mouse 78/59/39/24 (plan: stick 71/51/31/18, keyboard 88/70/47/28, mouse 95/82/59/36). My scripted person uses the same reaction on all devices, so this shows fairness, not a match to the plan's keyboard and mouse rows.\n   - No person can play here, so feel is judged by bots, scripted hands and frames only.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - `/goal` with args: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n   - Stop hook feedback 1: \"Not satisfied...\" (deliverables exist, but no full check against PLAN 21; cited step 3, No TODOs, untested items).\n   - Stop hook feedback 2: \"Not satisfied...\" (step 3 needed a captured run, not six static positions; CREDITS.md full scroll; browser coverage and WebKit iPhone shallow; balance and feel only with bots; Research and plan fields on partial evidence; \"the transcript does not establish completion\").\n   - No other human input.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Get the result of the final test run (`.scratch/full-test9.log`, background ID btphtmh0x).\n   - Remove the `void` placeholders added during audit 2, then re-run those tests. Known locations:\n     - `tests/headless/details.mjs`: `void inp;`, `void s;`, `void last;`, `void CLASSMATE_BARKS; void tick;` (also drop the unused imports).\n     - `tests/headless/_people.mjs`: `void st;`, `void lane; void eyes;`.\n     - Re-scan with `grep -rnE \"\\bvoid [a-zA-Z_]|TODO|FIXME\" src tools tests --include=*.mjs --include=*.js | grep -v credits-text`.\n   - Update `PROGRESS.md` (audit table and final count).\n   - Clean up: `rm -rf .scratch .shots .build .harness node_modules package-lock.json check` in the dev folder.\n   - Verify:\n     - html and exit-interview.json are present and the JSON parses, with no \"unknown\" answers.\n     - `sha256sum -c vendor/pixel-engine.sha256`.\n     - No processes of mine remain (check `/proc/*/exe` with cwd in my folder; pgrep -f matches my own shell).\n   - Send the final reply.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Waiting on the last full suite run after relaxing the Step note-count assertion. The previous run was 410/411, with only that assertion failing.\n\n   The final reply must include what the second audit found, the limits of this computer, the deviations, and these exact sections:\n\n   Deviations to report:\n   - Header solo is one wide lane with no classmates.\n   - Tray releases pills 3 at a time.\n   - Dev Tools' Balance and Games tabs scroll past the 8-row limit.\n   - Tray cups use distance checks rather than triggers.\n   - The hub pointer uses a ground-plane ray rather than `castRay` (invisible walls).\n\n   To re-run tests: `npm install` then `node tools/test.mjs`. Nothing is committed.\n\n   Source Information:\n   - Date: 2026-11-04 23:07:41\n   - Source: Wii Fit\n   - Plan: PLAN.md\n   - Genre and Perspective: fitness and balance minigame collection inside a light life-sim week (sports); isometric on the island, fixed front-on for class activities, other fixed views per activity (behind, side-on, top-down-ish)\n   - Tech: Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (riftlight engine kit) with three.js r186 and Rapier as bundled in it; esbuild 0.28.2 for packaging; vanilla JavaScript modules\n   - Art Direction: the engine's native pixel look (toon materials, 16-colour palette), with new models written as data for a spotless white island made of giant gym equipment\n   - Animation: engine ClipDefs with THREE.AnimationMixer, plus scrubbed reps, Squash, SpringChain and additive lean layers\n   - Audio: engine Song and SoundDef data plus a Web Audio formant voice, all code with no files; gibberish voices per speaker; music 10% by default\n   - Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1-4 players; Family Hour is local on one screen\n   - Testing: Headless Node playthroughs with bots, plus scripts playing through real keys, stick and mouse, one test command; Chromium, Firefox and WebKit with Playwright on file://; gamepad stub, phone profile, OfflineAudioContext and AnalyserNode checks; the hub harness; screenshots at 1920x1080 only for what a script cannot judge. No subagents for review\n   - Research: Read GUIDE.md, ASSETS.md and the hub README whole, searched API.md and the type files, and read the engine bundle for its font table and audio fields. No web research. The director's plan included engine and hub research and spikes\n   - Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n   - Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\n   - Usage: added on import\n\n   Testing Feedback:\n   1. About 70. Scripts caught about 30 (a crash, a dead activity, ghost messages that never reached other players, a save field lost on reload, a click that could not jump, hoops dropping before Go, and balance). Screenshots caught about 35 that scripts could not see (avatars vanishing, a dial hiding Ounce, prompts under dialogue). A line-by-line audit against the plan caught the rest (the 12 px safe margin, sample lines not verbatim, menus over the row limit, no Timeline in the ending).\n   2. Seven. Step Class avatars vanished from a bad ease name. Avatars folded into heaps from a lean that added up every frame. Vitamin Tray scored 0 for everyone because resting bodies slept through gravity changes. Step Class crashed on a mat colour. Online, ghosts never received their messages. Pier Jump could not be jumped with a mouse. Clicking on the island walked to the wrong place.\n   3. Scripts that play every activity through real keys, a real stick and a real mouse. Bots skip the input layer, so only these could find that a mouse could not jump at Pier Jump. Next came the bot sweep, which found a crash and gave every balance number, and the 1920x1080 contact sheets.\n   4. The WebKit and Firefox runs. Neither has WebGPU on this machine, so they only prove that the failure message shows.\n\n   Engine Feedback:\n   1. Headless in Node. The same game code, physics and mixers ran a full seven-day playthrough with bots in about a minute, so I could test the real game constantly. Models as data with checkModel came second.\n   2. Yes. A ClipDef key takes its own ease names (in, out), not the tween names, and outQuad baked NaN with validateClip and analyzeClip both silent: avatars vanished only when the clip played. I also hung a script awaiting a scene change in manual time, and lost Tray to Rapier bodies sleeping through a gravity change.\n   3. The Dot and its driver seam: one lean model that a person, a pad, a bot or a ghost can all drive, used by every activity, attract, the tests and online. Close behind, the HUD kit: mixed-case text, discs, rings, menus and prompts.\n   4. The HUD is only rects, text and sprites, with no circles or alpha. Dials are drawn as scanlines, and menu dimming borrows the transition uniform. Also, pads are merged into one, so Family Hour reads navigator.getGamepads itself.\n   5. none\n   6. Make validateClip reject an unknown ease name. It would have saved the worst bug of the run, and it is a small change.\n\n   Prompt Feedback:\n   1. The verified recipes in the plan. Knowing which numbers and calls were already proven meant I could spend the effort on the game, and the bot table let me check the core feel at once.\n   2. Coconut Header is listed for lane staging with classmates on side mats, but also gets a wider lane when solo; I made solo one wide lane. Bias values such as +.10 have no stated unit; I treated them as stick lean, multiplied by authority.\n   3. Keeping every screen readable at 480x270 with pad, keys and mouse all working, while a dozen activities share one HUD. Composition took several rounds of screenshots.\n   4. Say whether Header solo has classmates, and give the unit for bias. Ask for contact sheets of every screen as a step, and say that tests must play through the real input as well as with bots, since those two caught more than I expected.\n\n   Also state: Files are in `work/`: the html, `exit-interview.json`, the dev folder, `PROGRESS.md`.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue the stop-hook goal, where I left off with: \"I'll set a threshold the chart actually guarantees and run once more.\"\n   - Wait with `timeout 595 tail -f .scratch/full-test9.log </dev/null | grep -m1 \"^exit\"` from the dev folder, then read the tail of the log.\n   - If it is all green, remove the listed `void` lines from `tests/headless/details.mjs` and `tests/headless/_people.mjs` and re-run `node tools/test.mjs --fast details play`. A full re-run is only needed if game code or `src/data/about.js` changes; if so, rebuild, because the build writes the html and the exit interview.\n   - Then update PROGRESS.md, clean up, verify the deliverables and send the final reply with all required sections, stating the real test count.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (lik