{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QxYVRrL59ZuD8XJgvQd3go","type":"tool_result","content":"/engineFeedback/5 :: Make validateClip reject an unknown ease name. It would have saved t\n{\"name\": \"We Fit In\", \"tagline\": \"Keep the dot in the circle.\", \"description\": \"A week at a spotless wellness island run by a small, polite, deeply judgmental bathroom scale. Your whole body is one dot. Keep it in the circle.\", \"type\": \"Game\", \"genre\": \"Sports\", \"source\": \"Wii Fit\", \"series\": \"Wii Fit\", \"players\": \"1\\u20134\", \"controls\": \"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.\", \"tags\": [\"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"arcade\", \"3d\", \"s\n{\n\"date\": \"2026-11-04 23:07:41\",\n\"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n\"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n\"genre\": \"Fitness and balance minigame collection inside a light life-sim week (sports)\",\n\"perspective\": \"Isometric on the island; fixed front-on for class activities; other fixed views per activity (behind, side-on, top-down-ish)\",\n\"tech\": \"Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (riftlight engine kit) with three.js r186 and Rapier as bundled in it; esbuild 0.28.2 for packaging; vanilla JavaScript modules\",\n\"artDirection\": \"The engine's native pixel look (toon materials, 16-colour palette), with new models written as data for a spotless white island made of giant gym equipment\",\n\"animation\": \"Engine ClipDefs with THREE.AnimationMixer, plus scrubbed reps, Squash, SpringChain and additive lean layers\",\n\"audio\": \"Engine Song and SoundDef data plus a Web Audio formant voice: all code, no files. Gibberish voices per speaker. Music 10% by default\",\n\"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1-4 players; Family Hour is local on one screen\",\n\"testing\": \"Headless Node playthroughs with bots, plus scripts playing through real keys, stick and mouse, one test command; Chromium, Firefox and WebKit with Playwright on file://; gamepad stub, phone profile, OfflineAudioContext and AnalyserNode checks; the hub harness; screenshots at 1920x1080 only for what a script cannot judge. No subagents for review\",\n\"research\": \"Read GUIDE.md, ASSETS.md and the hub README whole, searched API.md and the type files, and read the engine\n{'sourceInformation': 15, 'testingFeedback': 4, 'engineFeedback': 6, 'promptFeedback': 4, 'aiHub': 10}\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in \n115:  \"aiHub\": {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"c4505ecf-7868-496b-83b4-28f97de233c7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:30:39.416Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/engineFeedback/5 :: Make validateClip reject an unknown ease name. It would have saved t\n{\"name\": \"We Fit In\", \"tagline\": \"Keep the dot in the circle.\", \"description\": \"A week at a spotless wellness island run by a small, polite, deeply judgmental bathroom scale. Your whole body is one dot. Keep it in the circle.\", \"type\": \"Game\", \"genre\": \"Sports\", \"source\": \"Wii Fit\", \"series\": \"Wii Fit\", \"players\": \"1\\u20134\", \"controls\": \"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.\", \"tags\": [\"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"arcade\", \"3d\", \"s\n{\n\"date\": \"2026-11-04 23:07:41\",\n\"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n\"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n\"genre\": \"Fitness and balance minigame collection inside a light life-sim week (sports)\",\n\"perspective\": \"Isometric on the island; fixed front-on for class activities; other fixed views per activity (behind, side-on, top-down-ish)\",\n\"tech\": \"Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (riftlight engine kit) with three.js r186 and Rapier as bundled in it; esbuild 0.28.2 for packaging; vanilla JavaScript modules\",\n\"artDirection\": \"The engine's native pixel look (toon materials, 16-colour palette), with new models written as data for a spotless white island made of giant gym equipment\",\n\"animation\": \"Engine ClipDefs with THREE.AnimationMixer, plus scrubbed reps, Squash, SpringChain and additive lean layers\",\n\"audio\": \"Engine Song and SoundDef data plus a Web Audio formant voice: all code, no files. Gibberish voices per speaker. Music 10% by default\",\n\"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1-4 players; Family Hour is local on one screen\",\n\"testing\": \"Headless Node playthroughs with bots, plus scripts playing through real keys, stick and mouse, one test command; Chromium, Firefox and WebKit with Playwright on file://; gamepad stub, phone profile, OfflineAudioContext and AnalyserNode checks; the hub harness; screenshots at 1920x1080 only for what a script cannot judge. No subagents for review\",\n\"research\": \"Read GUIDE.md, ASSETS.md and the hub README whole, searched API.md and the type files, and read the engine\n{'sourceInformation': 15, 'testingFeedback': 4, 'engineFeedback': 6, 'promptFeedback': 4, 'aiHub': 10}\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in \n115:  \"aiHub\": {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QxYVRrL59ZuD8XJgvQd3go","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
