{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjYmT9xCS3A2M11ZNzaY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012wGW9kQo4QcQV9sehtrUEA","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","offset":120,"limit":80},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4715,"cache_read_input_tokens":51605,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4715},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"ff7a815e-d140-4f90-a502-228c9ce5d94f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:31:26.799Z","request_id":"req_011CgjYmSfgHjhhfA7VaJ2mW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012wGW9kQo4QcQV9sehtrUEA":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","offset":120,"limit":80}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012wGW9kQo4QcQV9sehtrUEA","type":"tool_result","content":"120\t// src/core/dot.js: pure, no engine imports. Step in fixedUpdate at 60 Hz. p is in -1.2..1.2.\n121\texport class Dot {\n122\t  x = 0; y = 0; vx = 0; vy = 0; ux = 0; uy = 0; t = 0;\n123\t  constructor(rand) { this.ph = [rand(), rand(), rand(), rand()].map((r) => r * 6.283); }\n124\t  step(dt, inX, inY, T, m = {}) { // T: tunables. m: per-activity modifiers.\n125\t    this.t += dt;\n126\t    const k = Math.min(1, dt / T.dotLag);\n127\t    this.ux += (inX - this.ux) * k; this.uy += (inY - this.uy) * k;\n128\t    const n = T.dotNoise * (m.noise ?? 1), inst = T.dotInstability * (m.inst ?? 1), auth = T.dotAuthority * (m.auth ?? 1);\n129\t    const nx = n * (Math.sin(1.7 * this.t + this.ph[0]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(3.1 * this.t + this.ph[1]));\n130\t    const ny = n * (Math.sin(1.3 * this.t + this.ph[2]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(2.7 * this.t + this.ph[3]));\n131\t    this.vx += (inst * this.x + auth * this.ux - T.dotDamping * this.vx + nx + (m.bx ?? 0)) * dt;\n132\t    this.vy += (inst * this.y + auth * this.uy - T.dotDamping * this.vy + ny + (m.by ?? 0)) * dt;\n133\t    this.x += this.vx * dt; this.y += this.vy * dt;\n134\t    const d = Math.hypot(this.x, this.y);\n135\t    if (d > 1.2) { const s = 1.2 / d; this.x *= s; this.y *= s; this.vx *= 0.3; this.vy *= 0.3; }\n136\t  }\n137\t}\n138\t// Defaults: dotInstability 0.6, dotAuthority 3.0, dotDamping 3.4, dotNoise 0.8, dotLag 0.08\n139\t```\n140\t\n141\tTop speed is about 0.9 units/s, so a lean feels like shifting a heavy marble. Impulses (a sneeze, a gust) add directly to `vx`/`vy`.\n142\t\n143\t### Lean input\n144\t\n145\tAll devices produce one vector `u` in the unit disc, read per lane through a **driver** (section 16).\n146\t\n147\t| Device | `u` |\n148\t|---|---|\n149\t| Stick | `ctx.input.moveAxis()`; set `input.gamepadDeadzone = 0.12` |\n150\t| Keyboard | WASD / arrows, smoothed (attack 0.10 s, release 0.06 s). **Hold Shift for half lean.** |\n151\t| Mouse | Pointer offset from the dial's centre ÷ `mouseLeanRadius` (70 art px), clamped. It is a force, not a target, so you still have to balance. Draw a small crosshair and a line from dial to pointer. |\n152\t| Bot | Delayed PD controller (below) |\n153\t\n154\t### Bots ✔\n155\t\n156\tThe same bots drive classmates, attract mode and the tests:\n157\t\n158\t```\n159\teach step: seen = state tau seconds ago;  d += (rand-0.5)*err*dt*6;  d *= 0.995;\n160\t           u = -kp*(seen.p - target) - kd*seen.v + d;  clamp to the unit disc\n161\tsloppy  tau .42 kp .7  kd .12 err 1.3\n162\taverage tau .30 kp 1.1 kd .35 err .8\n163\tgood    tau .22 kp 1.5 kd .55 err .45\n164\texpert  tau .17 kp 1.9 kd .7  err .2\n165\t```\n166\t\n167\t**Measured time in ring ✔** (35 s, 40 seeds, first 2 s not counted):\n168\t\n169\t| Ring radius | .40 easy | .30 normal | .22 hard | .16 brutal |\n170\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n171\t| idle | 11% | 7% | 4% | 2% |\n172\t| sloppy | 21% | 13% | 7% | 4% |\n173\t| average | 71% | 51% | 31% | 18% |\n174\t| good | 100% | 93% | 74% | 49% |\n175\t| expert | 100% | 100% | 98% | 79% |\n176\t| keyboard, average | 88% | 70% | 47% | 28% |\n177\t| mouse, average | 95% | 82% | 59% | 36% |\n178\t\n179\t**Stars for Dot scores: 45 / 70 / 90.** So at ring .30, doing nothing gets no stars, an average player ★, a good one ★★★. Keep this shape if you retune; the test suite guards it (section 18).\n180\t\n181\t---\n182\t\n183\t## 5. Activities\n184\t\n185\t### Shared flow (`src/scenes/activity/base.js`)\n186\t\n187\t`intro` (camera glide, Coach's one line, a card with goal and controls for the current device) → `practice` (first time only: 8 s, unscored, \"Try it.\") → `countdown` → `play` → `outro` → **Results** (stars pop in one by one, score, Drips, a line chosen by activity and stars, classmates' scores) → Retry / Next / Back.\n188\t\n189\t- Each activity is a scene plus a data entry in `src/data/activities.js`: id, name, station, camera, song, tunables, star thresholds, unlock day, `hard` overrides, lines.\n190\t- No fail states. Falls cost points and dignity.\n191\t- **Each activity defines its bot play for a given skill** (circling at a set speed, pressing within a timing error, heading the nearest coconut). The Dot bots in section 4 cover the balance parts. Classmates, attract mode and the tests all use it.\n192\t- Every activity must be readable within 5 seconds with no text.\n193\t- **Hard versions** apply data overrides (smaller rings, faster tempo).\n194\t- **Lanes:** Holding Still, Reps, Hoop, Header and Step run in **lane staging**, up to 4 mats in a row, each with its own driver (local, bot or ghost). Solo play puts you on the centre mat with two classmates as bots.\n195\t\n196\t**Lane camera ✔ (3 mats):** `{ preset: 'fixed', position: [0, 2.3, 8.2], target: [0, 1.15, 0], fov: 30 }`, mats at x = -2.2, 0, 2.2, z = 0.8. **For 4 mats ✔:** position `[0, 3, 9.5]`, target `[0, 1, 0]`, fov 32, mats at x = -3, -1, 1, 3. Multiply the distance by `max(1, (16/9) / aspect)` so narrow windows don't clip the outer mats.\n197\t\n198\t**Staging rules ✔ (found in test renders):**\n199\t- Put Coach to one side of the player, not directly behind; their silhouettes merged."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"60b1de0b-5767-448e-baaa-c1463240b3b8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:31:26.810Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","content":"// src/core/dot.js: pure, no engine imports. Step in fixedUpdate at 60 Hz. p is in -1.2..1.2.\nexport class Dot {\n  x = 0; y = 0; vx = 0; vy = 0; ux = 0; uy = 0; t = 0;\n  constructor(rand) { this.ph = [rand(), rand(), rand(), rand()].map((r) => r * 6.283); }\n  step(dt, inX, inY, T, m = {}) { // T: tunables. m: per-activity modifiers.\n    this.t += dt;\n    const k = Math.min(1, dt / T.dotLag);\n    this.ux += (inX - this.ux) * k; this.uy += (inY - this.uy) * k;\n    const n = T.dotNoise * (m.noise ?? 1), inst = T.dotInstability * (m.inst ?? 1), auth = T.dotAuthority * (m.auth ?? 1);\n    const nx = n * (Math.sin(1.7 * this.t + this.ph[0]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(3.1 * this.t + this.ph[1]));\n    const ny = n * (Math.sin(1.3 * this.t + this.ph[2]) + 0.6 * Math.sin(2.7 * this.t + this.ph[3]));\n    this.vx += (inst * this.x + auth * this.ux - T.dotDamping * this.vx + nx + (m.bx ?? 0)) * dt;\n    this.vy += (inst * this.y + auth * this.uy - T.dotDamping * this.vy + ny + (m.by ?? 0)) * dt;\n    this.x += this.vx * dt; this.y += this.vy * dt;\n    const d = Math.hypot(this.x, this.y);\n    if (d > 1.2) { const s = 1.2 / d; this.x *= s; this.y *= s; this.vx *= 0.3; this.vy *= 0.3; }\n  }\n}\n// Defaults: dotInstability 0.6, dotAuthority 3.0, dotDamping 3.4, dotNoise 0.8, dotLag 0.08\n```\n\nTop speed is about 0.9 units/s, so a lean feels like shifting a heavy marble. Impulses (a sneeze, a gust) add directly to `vx`/`vy`.\n\n### Lean input\n\nAll devices produce one vector `u` in the unit disc, read per lane through a **driver** (section 16).\n\n| Device | `u` |\n|---|---|\n| Stick | `ctx.input.moveAxis()`; set `input.gamepadDeadzone = 0.12` |\n| Keyboard | WASD / arrows, smoothed (attack 0.10 s, release 0.06 s). **Hold Shift for half lean.** |\n| Mouse | Pointer offset from the dial's centre ÷ `mouseLeanRadius` (70 art px), clamped. It is a force, not a target, so you still have to balance. Draw a small crosshair and a line from dial to pointer. |\n| Bot | Delayed PD controller (below) |\n\n### Bots ✔\n\nThe same bots drive classmates, attract mode and the tests:\n\n```\neach step: seen = state tau seconds ago;  d += (rand-0.5)*err*dt*6;  d *= 0.995;\n           u = -kp*(seen.p - target) - kd*seen.v + d;  clamp to the unit disc\nsloppy  tau .42 kp .7  kd .12 err 1.3\naverage tau .30 kp 1.1 kd .35 err .8\ngood    tau .22 kp 1.5 kd .55 err .45\nexpert  tau .17 kp 1.9 kd .7  err .2\n```\n\n**Measured time in ring ✔** (35 s, 40 seeds, first 2 s not counted):\n\n| Ring radius | .40 easy | .30 normal | .22 hard | .16 brutal |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| idle | 11% | 7% | 4% | 2% |\n| sloppy | 21% | 13% | 7% | 4% |\n| average | 71% | 51% | 31% | 18% |\n| good | 100% | 93% | 74% | 49% |\n| expert | 100% | 100% | 98% | 79% |\n| keyboard, average | 88% | 70% | 47% | 28% |\n| mouse, average | 95% | 82% | 59% | 36% |\n\n**Stars for Dot scores: 45 / 70 / 90.** So at ring .30, doing nothing gets no stars, an average player ★, a good one ★★★. Keep this shape if you retune; the test suite guards it (section 18).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Activities\n\n### Shared flow (`src/scenes/activity/base.js`)\n\n`intro` (camera glide, Coach's one line, a card with goal and controls for the current device) → `practice` (first time only: 8 s, unscored, \"Try it.\") → `countdown` → `play` → `outro` → **Results** (stars pop in one by one, score, Drips, a line chosen by activity and stars, classmates' scores) → Retry / Next / Back.\n\n- Each activity is a scene plus a data entry in `src/data/activities.js`: id, name, station, camera, song, tunables, star thresholds, unlock day, `hard` overrides, lines.\n- No fail states. Falls cost points and dignity.\n- **Each activity defines its bot play for a given skill** (circling at a set speed, pressing within a timing error, heading the nearest coconut). The Dot bots in section 4 cover the balance parts. Classmates, attract mode and the tests all use it.\n- Every activity must be readable within 5 seconds with no text.\n- **Hard versions** apply data overrides (smaller rings, faster tempo).\n- **Lanes:** Holding Still, Reps, Hoop, Header and Step run in **lane staging**, up to 4 mats in a row, each with its own driver (local, bot or ghost). Solo play puts you on the centre mat with two classmates as bots.\n\n**Lane camera ✔ (3 mats):** `{ preset: 'fixed', position: [0, 2.3, 8.2], target: [0, 1.15, 0], fov: 30 }`, mats at x = -2.2, 0, 2.2, z = 0.8. **For 4 mats ✔:** position `[0, 3, 9.5]`, target `[0, 1, 0]`, fov 32, mats at x = -3, -1, 1, 3. Multiply the distance by `max(1, (16/9) / aspect)` so narrow windows don't clip the outer mats.\n\n**Staging rules ✔ (found in test renders):**\n- Put Coach to one side of the player, not directly behind; their silhouettes merged.","numLines":80,"startLine":120,"totalLines":993}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012wGW9kQo4QcQV9sehtrUEA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjYmT9xCS3A2M11ZNzaY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014HAnWtnoaCHjVL5pTtiPsK","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","offset":258,"limit":32},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4715,"cache_read_input_tokens":51605,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4715},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"7d4d8645-7968-49b1-989b-ba66bf192e56","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:31:27.849Z","request_id":"req_011CgjYmSfgHjhhfA7VaJ2mW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014HAnWtnoaCHjVL5pTtiPsK":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","offset":258,"limit":32}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014HAnWtnoaCHjVL5pTtiPsK","type":"tool_result","content":"258\t- Avatars step on platforms using the kit's `StepUp` / `StepDown` or your own. Classmates dance with occasional mistakes. Confetti at combo milestones.\n259\t\n260\t### 5.5 Coconut Header (Lagoon Games, balance)\n261\t\n262\tLean left and right along the sand. Dennis runs a catapult.\n263\t\n264\t- Lane ±2 m solo (±0.8 m in lanes). Speed 4.5 m/s × `u.x`.\n265\t- Objects land at head height after 1.4 s with a shadow telegraph, interval 1.3 s → 0.7 s. 70% coconut (head it: +10 × combo tier), 25% flip-flop (dodge it, or -10, combo lost, .6 s daze with circling stars), 5% golden pineapple (+30).\n266\t- Combo tiers ×2/×3/×4 at 5/10/20. 60 s. Stars 150/400/800.\n267\t- Hitstop .05 s on each header. Squash the head. Coconuts fly back at Dennis, who stops being fine.\n268\t\n269\t### 5.6 Slackline (Lagoon Games, balance)\n270\t\n271\tA sagging line across the lagoon between giant dumbbells. Camera low behind you.\n272\t\n273\t- **X is balance, forward is progress.** Push forward (`u.y > .3`) to walk at 1.1 m/s. Walking is less stable, so stopping to recover is a real choice.\n274\t- Defaults ✔ (simulated): effective instability 1.2 standing and 2.6 walking, so `m.inst = 1.2 / T.dotInstability` and `T.slackWalkInst / T.dotInstability`; `m.noise` 1.25; gusts every 6 m, `m.bx` ±1.6 for 1 s, telegraphed 1.5 s by flags and wind lines; fall at `|x| > 1`. Lock y (`dot.y = dot.vy = 0` after each step). Bots walk only while `|x| < .45`.\n275\t- Fall: 1.2 s of slow motion, splash, back to the checkpoint (0/10/20 m). Kevin lands on your head at 18 m and adds a bias until 24 m. 30 m, 75 s limit.\n276\t- Measured ✔: idle never finishes; sloppy rarely; average 38 s with 0.2 falls; good 28 s with 0 falls.\n277\t- **Stars:** ★ finish; ★★ ≤ 1 fall and under 45 s; ★★★ 0 falls and under 32 s. Score `1000 - 60 × falls - 8 × (time - 27)`.\n278\t- Sag the line under your feet (segments updated each frame). Arms out: the kit's `Tiptoe` plus T-pose arms set after the mixer, or a tuned `gaitClip`.\n279\t\n280\t### 5.7 Vitamin Tray (Lagoon Games, balance)\n281\t\n282\tTilt a lacquered tray to roll coloured vitamins into matching cups. Top-down-ish fixed camera.\n283\t\n284\t- **Tilt gravity, not the tray ✔:** the colliders stay flat and static; set `ctx.physics.world.gravity`; a visual `Group` tilts, with the vitamins as its children at `body.translation()`.\n285\t- **The engine's gravity is -24**, not -9.8. Use `trayGravity` 9.8 here and restore it on leaving. Max tilt 14°, driven by `u` with .12 s lag. Enable CCD on the balls.\n286\t- Cups are untagged cylinder triggers ✔ (they see dynamic bodies). 8 vitamins, 2-3 colours, 60 s. +10 correct, -3 wrong; rail gaps in later boards drop a vitamin (-1, respawns after 3 s).\n287\t- Three boards as ASCII in data (`#` wall, `.` floor, `o` start, `R`/`B`/`Y` cups). Stars at 40/60/80% of the board's maximum.\n288\t\n289\t### 5.8 Island Jog (Jogging Path, aerobics)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"f9afc129-30cf-4def-a883-a63c4508e235","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:31:27.856Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","content":"- Avatars step on platforms using the kit's `StepUp` / `StepDown` or your own. Classmates dance with occasional mistakes. Confetti at combo milestones.\n\n### 5.5 Coconut Header (Lagoon Games, balance)\n\nLean left and right along the sand. Dennis runs a catapult.\n\n- Lane ±2 m solo (±0.8 m in lanes). Speed 4.5 m/s × `u.x`.\n- Objects land at head height after 1.4 s with a shadow telegraph, interval 1.3 s → 0.7 s. 70% coconut (head it: +10 × combo tier), 25% flip-flop (dodge it, or -10, combo lost, .6 s daze with circling stars), 5% golden pineapple (+30).\n- Combo tiers ×2/×3/×4 at 5/10/20. 60 s. Stars 150/400/800.\n- Hitstop .05 s on each header. Squash the head. Coconuts fly back at Dennis, who stops being fine.\n\n### 5.6 Slackline (Lagoon Games, balance)\n\nA sagging line across the lagoon between giant dumbbells. Camera low behind you.\n\n- **X is balance, forward is progress.** Push forward (`u.y > .3`) to walk at 1.1 m/s. Walking is less stable, so stopping to recover is a real choice.\n- Defaults ✔ (simulated): effective instability 1.2 standing and 2.6 walking, so `m.inst = 1.2 / T.dotInstability` and `T.slackWalkInst / T.dotInstability`; `m.noise` 1.25; gusts every 6 m, `m.bx` ±1.6 for 1 s, telegraphed 1.5 s by flags and wind lines; fall at `|x| > 1`. Lock y (`dot.y = dot.vy = 0` after each step). Bots walk only while `|x| < .45`.\n- Fall: 1.2 s of slow motion, splash, back to the checkpoint (0/10/20 m). Kevin lands on your head at 18 m and adds a bias until 24 m. 30 m, 75 s limit.\n- Measured ✔: idle never finishes; sloppy rarely; average 38 s with 0.2 falls; good 28 s with 0 falls.\n- **Stars:** ★ finish; ★★ ≤ 1 fall and under 45 s; ★★★ 0 falls and under 32 s. Score `1000 - 60 × falls - 8 × (time - 27)`.\n- Sag the line under your feet (segments updated each frame). Arms out: the kit's `Tiptoe` plus T-pose arms set after the mixer, or a tuned `gaitClip`.\n\n### 5.7 Vitamin Tray (Lagoon Games, balance)\n\nTilt a lacquered tray to roll coloured vitamins into matching cups. Top-down-ish fixed camera.\n\n- **Tilt gravity, not the tray ✔:** the colliders stay flat and static; set `ctx.physics.world.gravity`; a visual `Group` tilts, with the vitamins as its children at `body.translation()`.\n- **The engine's gravity is -24**, not -9.8. Use `trayGravity` 9.8 here and restore it on leaving. Max tilt 14°, driven by `u` with .12 s lag. Enable CCD on the balls.\n- Cups are untagged cylinder triggers ✔ (they see dynamic bodies). 8 vitamins, 2-3 colours, 60 s. +10 correct, -3 wrong; rail gaps in later boards drop a vitamin (-1, respawns after 3 s).\n- Three boards as ASCII in data (`#` wall, `.` floor, `o` start, `R`/`B`/`Y` cups). Stars at 40/60/80% of the board's maximum.\n\n### 5.8 Island Jog (Jogging Path, aerobics)","numLines":32,"startLine":258,"totalLines":993}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014HAnWtnoaCHjVL5pTtiPsK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
