{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rh7Smgensz73fVFKJctYvR","type":"tool_result","content":"23:1. **You are a dot.** Almost everything is one verb: lean. The left stick, WASD or the mouse moves your centre of balance, and it has weight and sway. Poses, reps, hoops, slacklines and the finale are all different ways of moving or holding the Dot.\n32:| Your body is the controller; a centre-of-balance dot | The Dot: real sway physics on a stick, keys or mouse |\n150:| Keyboard | WASD / arrows, smoothed (attack 0.10 s, release 0.06 s). **Hold Shift for half lean.** |\n151:| Mouse | Pointer offset from the dial's centre ÷ `mouseLeanRadius` (70 art px), clamped. It is a force, not a target, so you still have to balance. Draw a small crosshair and a line from dial to pointer. |\n176:| keyboard, average | 88% | 70% | 47% | 28% |\n177:| mouse, average | 95% | 82% | 59% | 36% |\n218:- **Breath:** a bar rises and falls (\"In…\" / \"Out…\"). Hold R2 / Space / left mouse on In, release on Out. Keep a sync value `s` (0..1, smoothed), and `m.noise *= 1.25 - 0.55 * s`, so breathing well literally calms you.\n233:- **Keyboard uses rate control:** S/W move `r` at the target speed, no key holds it. Otherwise keys could only slam between ends.\n241:**Circle the stick** (or the mouse, or roll W-D-S-A) to keep hoops up.\n252:Footprints scroll to a hit line. Left foot: L1 or L2 / F or ← / left mouse button. Right foot: R1 or R2 / J or → / right mouse button.\n373:- **Mouse:** hovering a station highlights it and names it; clicking walks there and enters; clicking ground walks there (pointer ray via `camera.rayAt`, then `castRay`). Steer the hero by writing its `MoveInput.move`.\n436:**One UI for every device: the pixel HUD.** No DOM menus; same screens for pad, keyboard and mouse. Build a small kit in `src/ui/`.\n477:| Action | DualSense (Xbox glyph) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n482:| Pause | Options (Menu) | Esc, P | Pause icon, top right, shown while the mouse moves |\n490:- **Keep the mouse native:** the Dot follows the mouse as soon as the mouse moves, and goes back to stick or keys as soon as those are used.\n495:- Prompts always read `[glyph] verb` and follow the **last device used**. Track it in `src/core/device.js` from `ctx.input`: `held`/`queuedPresses` starting `Pad` or a stick past .3 means pad; `Mouse*` or pointer movement means mouse; anything else means keyboard. Add guarded DOM `keydown`/`poin\n496:- **Glyph sprites, drawn by you in `src/art/glyphs.js`:** PlayStation shapes ✕ ○ □ △ in their colours, L1 R1 L2 R2, Options, sticks. Xbox A B X Y (a Settings option), LB RB LT RT, Menu. Keycaps with the letter. A mouse with the used button lit.\n513:Music volume (**default 10%**), SFX, Voice, Button glyphs (PlayStation / Xbox), Gentle Mode (rings ×1.25, noise ×.8), Mouse lean radius, Step timing offset, Reduce flashes, Look (Default, `storybook`, `arcade`, `handheld`), Pixel size (`engine.settings.set({ look, pixelSize })`), Fullscreen, Res\n517:Detect ✔ `matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no gamepad. Start with `touch: false` always, and `settings: { button: 'top-right' }` only on such devices (otherwise `button: false`). ✔ The ⚙ appears and a tap opens the engine's panel. Show over the title: **\"Controller or keyb\n547:- **Any input exits**: key, click, mouse move past a few pixels, wheel, pad button or stick, touch. You return to the title and the timer re-arms.\n562:Join screen: **each device claims a mat by pressing Cross/Enter** (up to 4 pads plus keyboard-and-mouse). Bots can fill empty mats (toggle).\n577:<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J: step.\">\n789:- **Drivers** (`src/core/drivers.js`): `read(out)` fills `{ x, y, breath, stepL, stepR, confirm }`. `LocalDriver` (engine input and mouse), `PadDriver(index)` (Family Hour), `BotDriver(skill)`, `GhostDriver` (display only). Attract, tests, classmates and online all reuse this one seam.\n874:- `input.setPointer(x, y, true)` drives the mouse.\n902:15. Pad stub: ✕ confirms; prompts show PlayStation glyphs; the Settings option gives Xbox; a key press switches to keycaps; mouse move switches to mouse prompts; hover moves focus; click activates. Record each prompt state in `App.state()` so no picture is needed.\n904:17. Family Hour with 2 stub pads plus keyboard: three lanes move independently.\n936:**No TODOs, placeholders, stubs or dead menu items.** Every screen works with pad, keyboard and mouse.\n952:- `controls`: `Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.`\n986:| Controller first at 10 feet; native keyboard and mouse on the same screens | §9 |\n987:| Prompts follow last input; PlayStation glyphs; Xbox option; keys and mouse | §9, §18 test 15 |\n=====\n47:## 2. World and cast\n761:## 16. Architecture\n794:## 17. Verified recipes\n879:## 18. Testing\n916:## 19. Build order\n934:## 20. Finishing\n961:## 21. Brief coverage checklist\n=====\n32:function ringTime(skill, ring = 0.3, seeds = 40) {\n41:      if (i >= 120) { n++; if (Math.hypot(d.x, d.y) <= ring) inside++; }\n48:await test('dot: idle bot under 20% at ring .30', () => assert(ringTime('idle') < 20));\n49:await test('dot: average bot 35-65% at ring .30', () => { const v = ringTime('average'); assert(v > 35 && v < 65, `${v}`); });\n50:await test('dot: good bot over 80% at ring .30', () => assert(ringTime('good') > 80));\n51:await test('dot: expert bot over 95% at ring .30', () => assert(ringTime('expert') > 95));\n112:const SAMPLES = [\"Hello! I'm Ounce. Please step on me.\", 'Ow.', \"That was a joke. I can't feel pain. I can only keep records.\", 'How old do you feel? This is not binding.', \"Your Wobble Age is 68. Is that close? No? \n121:await test('every character of every string has a glyph', () => {\n122:  const strings = [...allLines().map((l) => l.text), ...Object.values(ACTIVITIES).map((a) => a.name), ...Object.values(STATIONS).map((s) => s.name), ...MILESTONES.map((m) => m.name), ...Object.values(SOURCE_INFO), ..\n123:  for (const s of strings) for (const ch of s) assert(hasGlyph(ch) || ch === '\\n', `no glyph for \"${ch}\" in: ${s}`);\n134:  for (const k of ['date', 'source', 'plan', 'genre', 'perspective', 'tech', 'artDirection', 'animation', 'audio', 'online', 'testing', 'research', 'environment', 'model', 'usage']) assert(typeof e.sourceInformation[\n137:  for (const k of ['name', 'tagline', 'description', 'type', 'genre', 'source', 'series', 'players', 'controls']) assert(typeof AI_HUB[k] === 'string' && AI_HUB[k].length, k);\n143:await test('voice: syllabify is stable and the same word gives the same syllables', () => {\n146:  eq(JSON.stringify(a), JSON.stringify(b));\n=====\ntests/headless/play.mjs:10:const DEVICES = ['pad', 'keyboard', 'mouse'];","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"7a529bfa-8e2b-4160-baa9-af02e6a74ae8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:31:48.171Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"23:1. **You are a dot.** Almost everything is one verb: lean. The left stick, WASD or the mouse moves your centre of balance, and it has weight and sway. Poses, reps, hoops, slacklines and the finale are all different ways of moving or holding the Dot.\n32:| Your body is the controller; a centre-of-balance dot | The Dot: real sway physics on a stick, keys or mouse |\n150:| Keyboard | WASD / arrows, smoothed (attack 0.10 s, release 0.06 s). **Hold Shift for half lean.** |\n151:| Mouse | Pointer offset from the dial's centre ÷ `mouseLeanRadius` (70 art px), clamped. It is a force, not a target, so you still have to balance. Draw a small crosshair and a line from dial to pointer. |\n176:| keyboard, average | 88% | 70% | 47% | 28% |\n177:| mouse, average | 95% | 82% | 59% | 36% |\n218:- **Breath:** a bar rises and falls (\"In…\" / \"Out…\"). Hold R2 / Space / left mouse on In, release on Out. Keep a sync value `s` (0..1, smoothed), and `m.noise *= 1.25 - 0.55 * s`, so breathing well literally calms you.\n233:- **Keyboard uses rate control:** S/W move `r` at the target speed, no key holds it. Otherwise keys could only slam between ends.\n241:**Circle the stick** (or the mouse, or roll W-D-S-A) to keep hoops up.\n252:Footprints scroll to a hit line. Left foot: L1 or L2 / F or ← / left mouse button. Right foot: R1 or R2 / J or → / right mouse button.\n373:- **Mouse:** hovering a station highlights it and names it; clicking walks there and enters; clicking ground walks there (pointer ray via `camera.rayAt`, then `castRay`). Steer the hero by writing its `MoveInput.move`.\n436:**One UI for every device: the pixel HUD.** No DOM menus; same screens for pad, keyboard and mouse. Build a small kit in `src/ui/`.\n477:| Action | DualSense (Xbox glyph) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n482:| Pause | Options (Menu) | Esc, P | Pause icon, top right, shown while the mouse moves |\n490:- **Keep the mouse native:** the Dot follows the mouse as soon as the mouse moves, and goes back to stick or keys as soon as those are used.\n495:- Prompts always read `[glyph] verb` and follow the **last device used**. Track it in `src/core/device.js` from `ctx.input`: `held`/`queuedPresses` starting `Pad` or a stick past .3 means pad; `Mouse*` or pointer movement means mouse; anything else means keyboard. Add guarded DOM `keydown`/`poin\n496:- **Glyph sprites, drawn by you in `src/art/glyphs.js`:** PlayStation shapes ✕ ○ □ △ in their colours, L1 R1 L2 R2, Options, sticks. Xbox A B X Y (a Settings option), LB RB LT RT, Menu. Keycaps with the letter. A mouse with the used button lit.\n513:Music volume (**default 10%**), SFX, Voice, Button glyphs (PlayStation / Xbox), Gentle Mode (rings ×1.25, noise ×.8), Mouse lean radius, Step timing offset, Reduce flashes, Look (Default, `storybook`, `arcade`, `handheld`), Pixel size (`engine.settings.set({ look, pixelSize })`), Fullscreen, Res\n517:Detect ✔ `matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no gamepad. Start with `touch: false` always, and `settings: { button: 'top-right' }` only on such devices (otherwise `button: false`). ✔ The ⚙ appears and a tap opens the engine's panel. Show over the title: **\"Controller or keyb\n547:- **Any input exits**: key, click, mouse move past a few pixels, wheel, pad button or stick, touch. You return to the title and the timer re-arms.\n562:Join screen: **each device claims a mat by pressing Cross/Enter** (up to 4 pads plus keyboard-and-mouse). Bots can fill empty mats (toggle).\n577:<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J: step.\">\n789:- **Drivers** (`src/core/drivers.js`): `read(out)` fills `{ x, y, breath, stepL, stepR, confirm }`. `LocalDriver` (engine input and mouse), `PadDriver(index)` (Family Hour), `BotDriver(skill)`, `GhostDriver` (display only). Attract, tests, classmates and online all reuse this one seam.\n874:- `input.setPointer(x, y, true)` drives the mouse.\n902:15. Pad stub: ✕ confirms; prompts show PlayStation glyphs; the Settings option gives Xbox; a key press switches to keycaps; mouse move switches to mouse prompts; hover moves focus; click activates. Record each prompt state in `App.state()` so no picture is needed.\n904:17. Family Hour with 2 stub pads plus keyboard: three lanes move independently.\n936:**No TODOs, placeholders, stubs or dead menu items.** Every screen works with pad, keyboard and mouse.\n952:- `controls`: `Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.`\n986:| Controller first at 10 feet; native keyboard and mouse on the same screens | §9 |\n987:| Prompts follow last input; PlayStation glyphs; Xbox option; keys and mouse | §9, §18 test 15 |\n=====\n47:## 2. World and cast\n761:## 16. Architecture\n794:## 17. Verified recipes\n879:## 18. Testing\n916:## 19. Build order\n934:## 20. Finishing\n961:## 21. Brief coverage checklist\n=====\n32:function ringTime(skill, ring = 0.3, seeds = 40) {\n41:      if (i >= 120) { n++; if (Math.hypot(d.x, d.y) <= ring) inside++; }\n48:await test('dot: idle bot under 20% at ring .30', () => assert(ringTime('idle') < 20));\n49:await test('dot: average bot 35-65% at ring .30', () => { const v = ringTime('average'); assert(v > 35 && v < 65, `${v}`); });\n50:await test('dot: good bot over 80% at ring .30', () => assert(ringTime('good') > 80));\n51:await test('dot: expert bot over 95% at ring .30', () => assert(ringTime('expert') > 95));\n112:const SAMPLES = [\"Hello! I'm Ounce. Please step on me.\", 'Ow.', \"That was a joke. I can't feel pain. I can only keep records.\", 'How old do you feel? This is not binding.', \"Your Wobble Age is 68. Is that close? No? \n121:await test('every character of every string has a glyph', () => {\n122:  const strings = [...allLines().map((l) => l.text), ...Object.values(ACTIVITIES).map((a) => a.name), ...Object.values(STATIONS).map((s) => s.name), ...MILESTONES.map((m) => m.name), ...Object.values(SOURCE_INFO), ..\n123:  for (const s of strings) for (const ch of s) assert(hasGlyph(ch) || ch === '\\n', `no glyph for \"${ch}\" in: ${s}`);\n134:  for (const k of ['date', 'source', 'plan', 'genre', 'perspective', 'tech', 'artDirection', 'animation', 'audio', 'online', 'testing', 'research', 'environment', 'model', 'usage']) assert(typeof e.sourceInformation[\n137:  for (const k of ['name', 'tagline', 'description', 'type', 'genre', 'source', 'series', 'players', 'controls']) assert(typeof AI_HUB[k] === 'string' && AI_HUB[k].length, k);\n143:await test('voice: syllabify is stable and the same word gives the same syllables', () => {\n146:  eq(JSON.stringify(a), JSON.stringify(b));\n=====\ntests/headless/play.mjs:10:const DEVICES = ['pad', 'keyboard', 'mouse'];","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Rh7Smgensz73fVFKJctYvR","permission_decision":{"decision