{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019GK2V67fL5nHie3GUEZG2w","type":"tool_result","content":"== API: triggers / castRay\nAPI.md:11:5. Physics: `BoxOptions`, `Breakable`, `BreakableOptions`, `Breakables`, `BridgeOptions`, `Built`, `chain`, `ChainOptions`, `CharacterAnim`, `CharacterController`, `CharacterOptions`, `Chunk`, `clothGrid`, `ClothOptions`, `Crumble`, `CrumbleOptions`,\nAPI.md:286:- `dispose?(ctx: GameContext): void`: Called when the game is unloaded (`engine.loadGame(other)` or `engine.dispose()`), before the engine removes its scene objects, physics bodies, triggers, particles, HUD and music. Free anything else the game own\nAPI.md:1809:- `castRay(from: Vector3, dir: Vector3, maxDistance: number, ignoreTags: readonly string[] = NO_TAGS, exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): { distance: number; collider: RAPIER.Collider; normal: Vector3; point: Vector3 } | null`: Ray cast returning distance\nAPI.md:1813:- `trigger(shape: TriggerShape, at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, options: TriggerOptions = {}): Trigger`: A trigger volume with enter/exit callbacks (pickups, checkpoints, kill zones, doors). Checked after every fixed step against d\nAPI.md:1814:- `updateTriggers(): void`: Run every trigger's overlap query now (Physics.update does this after each step).\nAPI.md:1816:- `remove(target: RAPIER.RigidBody | RAPIER.Collider): void`: Remove a rigid body (with its colliders and any bound Object3D binding) or a single collider. Removing a collider whose fixed body has no other colliders removes that body too (what `add\nAPI.md:1817:- `clear(): void`: Empty the world: every body, collider, joint, character and vehicle controller, trigger, tag, binding, mover, field and belt goes; gravity and the solver's iterations go back to their defaults, the step accumulator and the step c\nAPI.md:1819:- `counts(): { bodies: number; colliders: number; joints: number; tags: number; bindings: number; triggers: number; controllers: number; vehicles: number; movers: number; fields: number; belts: number; }`: Sizes of everything Physics tracks (leak c\nAPI.md:1987:### class Trigger\nAPI.md:1991:trigger never blocks the character controller, ray casts or camera rays.\nAPI.md:1992:Create with `physics.trigger(shape, at, options)`.\nAPI.md:1994:- `new Trigger(def: TriggerShape, at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, options: TriggerOptions, accept: (c: RAPIER.Collider) => boolean, detach: (t: Trigger) => void)`\nAPI.md:1997:- `enabled: boolean`: A disabled trigger reports nothing (everything inside exits on the next step).\nAPI.md:2000:- `readonly def: TriggerShape`\nAPI.md:2001:- `readonly options: TriggerOptions`\nAPI.md:2006:### interface TriggerOptions\nAPI.md:2008:- `onEnter?(other: RAPIER.Collider, trigger: Trigger): void`: Called once when a collider starts overlapping the volume.\nAPI.md:2009:- `onExit?(other: RAPIER.Collider, trigger: Trigger): void`: Called once when it stops overlapping (or leaves the world).\nAPI.md:2013:- `once?: boolean`: Remove the trigger after its first enter (pickups).\nAPI.md:2016:### type TriggerShape\nAPI.md:2019:type TriggerShape = | { box: [number, number, number] } | { sphere: number } | { capsule: { halfHeight: number; radius: number } } | { cylinder: { halfHeight: number; radius: number } }\nAPI.md:2022:Trigger volume shape (half extents / radius in world units).\nGUIDE.md:61:| `async setup(ctx)` | once | build the level: meshes, colliders, models, characters, triggers |\nGUIDE.md:124:    // Coins: a model, spinning; a trigger volume collects it when the hero walks in.\nGUIDE.md:132:      physics.trigger({ cylinder: { halfHeight: 0.6, radius: 0.5 } }, [x, y, z], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.collect(ctx, item) });\nGUIDE.md:223:`loadGame` can be called from anywhere (a trigger, `update`); the swap happens after the\nGUIDE.md:224:frame. It unloads the old game: scene objects, physics, triggers, particles, HUD, music and\nGUIDE.md:295:### Physics queries and triggers\nGUIDE.md:298:const t = ctx.physics.trigger({ box: [1, 1.5, 0.5] }, [x, y, z], {\nGUIDE.md:304:ctx.physics.castRay(from, dir, maxDistance);    // { distance, collider, normal, point } | null\n== types files\nbundle.d.ts\nengine\ngame\ntypes/engine/physics/Physics.d.ts\ntypes/engine/index.d.ts:30:export { Physics, RAPIER, FIXED_DT, Trigger, type BoxOptions, type PhysicsState, type TriggerOptions, type TriggerShape } from './physics/Physics';\ntypes/engine/physics/Physics.d.ts:5:import { Trigger, type TriggerOptions, type TriggerShape } from './Trigger';\ntypes/engine/physics/Physics.d.ts:6:export { RAPIER, Trigger, type TriggerOptions, type TriggerShape };\ntypes/engine/physics/Physics.d.ts:149:    castRay(from: Vector3, dir: Vector3, maxDistance: number, ignoreTags?: readonly string[], exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): {\ntypes/engine/physics/Physics.d.ts:190:    trigger(shape: TriggerShape, at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, options?: TriggerOptions): Trigger;\ntypes/engine/physics/Trigger.d.ts:19:export interface TriggerOptions {\ntypes/engine/physics/Trigger.d.ts:43:    readonly options: TriggerOptions;\ntypes/engine/physics/Trigger.d.ts:59:    constructor(def: TriggerShape, at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, options: TriggerOptions, accept: (c: RAPIER.Collider) => boolean, detach: (t: Trigger) => void);\n== hub lines 50-70\n    if (Math.abs(z - 3) < 1.4 && Math.abs(x) < 15.2) return false;\n    if (Math.abs(x) < 1.4 && z > 6 && z < 13) return false;\n    return true;\n  }, 3000);\n  if (walls) {\n    for (const [pos, half] of [\n      [[0, 2, -ISLAND.halfZ - 0.2], [ISLAND.halfX + 1, 3, 0.4]], [[0, 2, ISLAND.halfZ + 0.2], [ISLAND.halfX + 1, 3, 0.4]],\n      [[-ISLAND.halfX + 0.2, 2, 0], [0.4, 3, ISLAND.halfZ + 1]], [[ISLAND.halfX + 0.2, 2, 0], [0.4, 3, ISLAND.halfZ + 1]],\n      [[17.2, 2, 1.5], [0.3, 3, 3.5]], [[19.5, 2, -2.2], [2.5, 3, 0.3]], [[19.5, 2, 5.2], [2.5, 3, 0.3]],\n    ]) physics.addStaticBox({ position: pos, halfExtents: half });\n  }\n  // Stations.\n  place(ctx, 'dais', { at: [0, -0.42, 3], scale: 1.4 });\n  const solid = (at, r) => physics.addStaticCylinder([at[0], 1.5, at[1]], 1.5, r);\n  place(ctx, 'pavilion', { at: [-11, 0, 3], palette: { roof: 'sky' } });\n  for (const a of [[-13.7, 1.4], [-13.7, 4.6], [-8.3, 1.4], [-8.3, 4.6]]) solid(a, 0.35);\n  place(ctx, 'rep-shed', { at: [11, 0, 1.6], collide: true });\n  place(ctx, 'giant-dumbbell', { at: [7.2, 0, 0.4], yaw: 30 });\n  place(ctx, 'beat-stage', { at: [12, 0, -11.6] });\n  physics.addStaticBox({ position: [12, 0.25, -11.6], halfExtents: [4, 0.25, 2.2] });\n  place(ctx, 'pier', { at: [-9.4, -1.1, -16], params: { len: 16 } });\n== hub lines 405-455\n    const { input } = ctx;\n    const dev = App.device;\n    this.hoverStation = null;\n    // The mouse: hover names a station, a click walks there; ground just walks.\n    if (dev.last === 'mouse') {\n      const hit = this.groundAtPointer(ctx);\n      if (hit) {\n        this.hoverStation = this.stationAtPointer();\n        if (input.wasPressed('MouseLeft')) {\n          this.walkTarget = { x: hit.x, z: hit.z };\n          this.autoEnter = this.hoverStation;\n          if (this.hoverStation) { const st = STATIONS[this.hoverStation]; this.walkTarget = { x: st.at[0], z: st.at[1] }; }\n          if (this.hoverStation && this.nearest === this.hoverStation) { this.autoEnter = null; this.walkTarget = null; this.activate(this.hoverStation); return; }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    if (this.nearest && input.wasPressed(...CONFIRM)) this.activate(this.nearest);\n  }\n\n  groundAtPointer(ctx) {\n    const p = ctx.input.pointer;\n    ctx.camera.rayAt(p.x, p.y, this.rayO, this.rayD);\n    if (this.rayD.y > -1e-4) return null;\n    // To the ground itself: castRay would stop at the invisible walls round the island, and the camera is outside them.\n    return this.pointOnRay(0.06);\n  }\n\n  pointOnRay(y) {\n    return this.rayO.clone().addScaledVector(this.rayD, (y - this.rayO.y) / this.rayD.y);\n  }\n\n  /** What's under the pointer: a station's body as well as its footprint, since they're tall and you point at the roof. */\n  stationAtPointer() {\n    let best = null, bestD = Infinity;\n    for (const y of [0.06, 1, 2, 3]) {\n      const p = this.pointOnRay(y);\n      for (const id of STATION_IDS) {\n        const st = STATIONS[id];\n        const d = Math.hypot(p.x - st.at[0], p.z - st.at[1]) / st.radius;\n        if (d < 0.85 && d < bestD) { bestD = d; best = id; }\n      }\n    }\n    return best;\n  }\n\n  activate(id) {\n    const st = STATIONS[id];\n    App.sfx('menuConfirm');\n    switch (st.kind) {\n      case 'menu': App.stack.push(new StationScreen(id, this)); break;\n      case 'scene': App.go(st.scene, { from: id }); break;\n== boards\n// Vitamin Tray boards, ASCII. # wall, . floor, o start, R B Y cups, _ a gap in the rail.\nexport const BOARDS = [\n  { name: 'Morning Dose', count: 8, active: 3, rows: [\n    '##############',\n    '#R....oo....B#',\n    '#............#',\n    '#....####....#',\n    '#............#',\n    '#B....oo....R#',\n    '##############',\n  ] },\n  { name: 'Second Opinion', count: 8, active: 3, rows: [\n    '##############',\n    '#R..#....#..B#',\n    '#...#.oo.#...#',\n    '#............#',\n    '#...#.oo.#...#',\n    '#Y..#....#..R#',\n    '##__######__##',\n  ] },\n  { name: 'Full Prescription', count: 8, active: 3, rows: [\n    '#####_###_####',\n    '#R....#.....B#',\n    '#.oo..#..##..#',\n    '#.....#......#',\n    '#..##...#.oo.#',\n    '#Y......#...R#',\n    '####_###_#####',\n  ] },\n];\nexport const TRAY_CELL = 0.5;\n== tray in data\n21:  tray: { name: 'Vitamin Tray', station: 'lagoon', scene: 'tray', song: 'lagoon', stars: 'percent', starPct: [40, 60, 80], unit: 'pts', day: 4, camera: 'tray', hard: { time: 0.8 }, coach: 'Your vitamins. Into the right cups. All of them,\n40:  tray: { dennis: 20, june: 52, marguerite: 70 }, pier: { dennis: 14, june: 27, marguerite: 41 },