{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AD6pDYujuizWDtyqV6fNmh","type":"tool_result","content":"86:1. **Morning Weigh-In** (about 45 s, section 6): balance test, one absurd question, today's Wobble Age.\n89:4. **Evening Report** (about 20 s): minutes, Drips, stars, the chart, tomorrow's \"concern\", new unlocks. The light goes to dusk (`applySky(engine, skyAt(19))`), then fade to morning.\n117:### The model ✔ (simulated with human-like bots; these are the defaults)\n167:**Measured time in ring ✔** (35 s, 40 seeds, first 2 s not counted):\n179:**Stars for Dot scores: 45 / 70 / 90.** So at ring .30, doing nothing gets no stars, an average player ★, a good one ★★★. Keep this shape if you retune; the test suite guards it (section 18).\n234:- **Rep quality:** `1 - 1.6 × mean|r - target|`, shown as Perfect ≥ .85, Good ≥ .65, else Wobbly. Score = mean × 100. Stars 55/75/90.\n254:- 104 BPM, 32 bars (about 74 s): intro 4, verse 8, chorus 8, breakdown 4, final 8. Charts are strings in data: `L.R.L.R.`.\n255:- Windows: Perfect ±55 ms, Good ±100, OK ±140 (scale `stepWindow`). Accuracy = (P + .7G + .4O) / N. Stars 55/75/90.\n274:- Defaults ✔ (simulated): effective instability 1.2 standing and 2.6 walking, so `m.inst = 1.2 / T.dotInstability` and `T.slackWalkInst / T.dotInstability`; `m.noise` 1.25; gusts every 6 m, `m.bx` ±1.6 for 1 s, telegraphed 1.5 s by flags and wind lines; fa\n276:- Measured ✔: idle never finishes; sloppy rarely; average 38 s with 0.2 falls; good 28 s with 0 falls.\n294:- Coach paces you on a white mobility scooter at exactly target speed, 3 m/s. Path about 220 m on a Catmull-Rom curve (about 75 s). More than 12 m behind, she waits, unimpressed.\n545:- **Playlist:** Hub walk → Holding Still → Hoop → Header → Step → Slackline → Tray → Pier Jump → Jog → Long Stand excerpt, about 14 s each, with iris transitions. Cover every activity and feature family.\n558:Three events in fixed windows: Stillness (a pose), then Beat (Reps or Hoop or Step), then Balance-lean (Header), each 55 s with 10 s between, about 3.2 minutes. The specific picks and shortened durations live in `src/data/medley.js`, and the picks come fro\n796:### Single-file build ✔ (boots on `file://` in about 1.3 s; passes `check.mjs` and the harness)\n816:The session client goes in **unmodified**: the hub replaces an unmodified copy with each new version. Nothing is fetched at runtime, so the game needs no CDN. Bundling doesn't count as editing the engine; `pixel-engine.js` itself stays byte-identical. Outp\n871:- 600 frames with mixers takes about 80 ms, and boot about 240 ms, so full playthroughs are cheap.\n888:4. **Every activity:** idle bot finishes with 0★ and no error; expert bot ≥ 2★ (≥ 3★ on easy ones); sloppy < expert; result written; Drips correct.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"d5d26e44-0fee-41e6-9bd4-dd0275199779","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:54:00.769Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"86:1. **Morning Weigh-In** (about 45 s, section 6): balance test, one absurd question, today's Wobble Age.\n89:4. **Evening Report** (about 20 s): minutes, Drips, stars, the chart, tomorrow's \"concern\", new unlocks. The light goes to dusk (`applySky(engine, skyAt(19))`), then fade to morning.\n117:### The model ✔ (simulated with human-like bots; these are the defaults)\n167:**Measured time in ring ✔** (35 s, 40 seeds, first 2 s not counted):\n179:**Stars for Dot scores: 45 / 70 / 90.** So at ring .30, doing nothing gets no stars, an average player ★, a good one ★★★. Keep this shape if you retune; the test suite guards it (section 18).\n234:- **Rep quality:** `1 - 1.6 × mean|r - target|`, shown as Perfect ≥ .85, Good ≥ .65, else Wobbly. Score = mean × 100. Stars 55/75/90.\n254:- 104 BPM, 32 bars (about 74 s): intro 4, verse 8, chorus 8, breakdown 4, final 8. Charts are strings in data: `L.R.L.R.`.\n255:- Windows: Perfect ±55 ms, Good ±100, OK ±140 (scale `stepWindow`). Accuracy = (P + .7G + .4O) / N. Stars 55/75/90.\n274:- Defaults ✔ (simulated): effective instability 1.2 standing and 2.6 walking, so `m.inst = 1.2 / T.dotInstability` and `T.slackWalkInst / T.dotInstability`; `m.noise` 1.25; gusts every 6 m, `m.bx` ±1.6 for 1 s, telegraphed 1.5 s by flags and wind lines; fa\n276:- Measured ✔: idle never finishes; sloppy rarely; average 38 s with 0.2 falls; good 28 s with 0 falls.\n294:- Coach paces you on a white mobility scooter at exactly target speed, 3 m/s. Path about 220 m on a Catmull-Rom curve (about 75 s). More than 12 m behind, she waits, unimpressed.\n545:- **Playlist:** Hub walk → Holding Still → Hoop → Header → Step → Slackline → Tray → Pier Jump → Jog → Long Stand excerpt, about 14 s each, with iris transitions. Cover every activity and feature family.\n558:Three events in fixed windows: Stillness (a pose), then Beat (Reps or Hoop or Step), then Balance-lean (Header), each 55 s with 10 s between, about 3.2 minutes. The specific picks and shortened durations live in `src/data/medley.js`, and the picks come fro\n796:### Single-file build ✔ (boots on `file://` in about 1.3 s; passes `check.mjs` and the harness)\n816:The session client goes in **unmodified**: the hub replaces an unmodified copy with each new version. Nothing is fetched at runtime, so the game needs no CDN. Bundling doesn't count as editing the engine; `pixel-engine.js` itself stays byte-identical. Outp\n871:- 600 frames with mixers takes about 80 ms, and boot about 240 ms, so full playthroughs are cheap.\n888:4. **Every activity:** idle bot finishes with 0★ and no error; expert bot ≥ 2★ (≥ 3★ on easy ones); sloppy < expert; result written; Drips correct.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AD6pDYujuizWDtyqV6fNmh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
