{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FxkjzAuStMmQzuARnJCKxL","type":"tool_result","content":"333\t## 6. Weigh-In and Wobble Age\n334\t\n335\tYour avatar steps onto Ounce (\"Ow.\" every time; the delivery varies). Close-up, huge dial, tiny animated needle.\n336\t\n337\t| Test | Rules (12-15 s) | Result T (0..1) |\n338\t|---|---|---|\n339\t| Stillness | Ring .30. Dot and ring fade after 3 s: \"Eyes closed.\" | in-ring fraction |\n340\t| Lean | Three targets (\"70% left\"). Reach and hold ±.1 for 1.5 s each. | based on time |\n341\t| Chase | Follow a slow target on a Lissajous path | 1 - mean distance × 2 |\n342\t\n343\tThen one question (section 8), then the reveal: the needle spins, the number rolls, Ounce remarks.\n344\t\n345\t```\n346\ttrue  = round(20 + 60 × (1 - mean(last 3 T))) - min(20, totalStars × 0.5), clamped to 18..95\n347\tshown = true + 7 until the confession, then true\n348\t```\n349\t\n350\tThe chart draws 7 points. At the confession every point animates down by 7. Test it: an expert bot ends lower than an average one, an idle bot stays high, and the confession subtracts exactly 7.\n351\t\n352\t---\n353\t\n354\t## 7. The island hub\n355\t\n356\t`iso` camera ✔ (`{ preset: 'iso', zoom: 1.15 }`) with `PlatformerCharacter` and the kit's full moveset. Jumping and waving have no purpose and should still be there. Island about 44 × 34 m. The top of the screen is -x, -z: **put tall things in that quadrant** so they never hide the player.\n357\t\n358\t| Place | Near (x, z) | Purpose |\n359\t|---|---|---|\n360\t| Weigh-In Terrace | (0, 3) | Day start, Ounce's dais |\n361\t| Pavilion of Holding Still | (-11, 3), sky-blue roof | Poses |\n362\t| The Rep Shed | (11, 3), orange roof | Reps |\n363\t| Beat Beach | (12, -10), on sand | Hoop, Step |\n364\t| Lagoon Games | (-12, -10), pier | Header, Slackline, Tray, Pier Jump |\n365\t| Jogging Path gate | (0, 11) | Island Jog |\n366\t| Sweat Jar | (4, -4) | Drips, milestones |\n367\t| Locker Room | (-4, -4) | Avatar |\n368\t| Hall of Numbers | (0, -8) | Records, chart, calendar |\n369\t| Hammock between palms | (14, 10) | End the day |\n370\t| Scenery | | Kettlebell Volcano (-15, -14), Foam Roller Hills (15, -14), Dumbbell Bridge over an inlet, medicine balls, gulls (`Boids`) overhead |\n371\t\n372\t- **Interaction:** a trigger shows `[✕] Enter: Pavilion of Holding Still`. Confirm opens a station menu: activities with stars and best score, locked rows greyed with the unlock day, one remark.\n373\t- **Mouse:** hovering a station highlights it and names it; clicking walks there and enters; clicking ground walks there (pointer ray via `camera.rayAt`, then `castRay`). Steer the hero by writing its `MoveInput.move`.\n374\t- **HUD:** day top-left, Drips top-right, today's prescription under the day, prompts bottom. Nothing else.\n375\t- **Ounce** hops after you (`Squash`, tween) and barks at most every 6 s.\n376\t- **Life:** classmates around the island doing small loops (stretching, sitting, failing).\n377\t\n378\t---\n379\t\n380\t## 8. Writing\n381\t\n382\t**Voice:** short declarative sentences. Polite, clinical, caring, faintly wounding. A remark should sound like it came from a nurse who has read your file. Understatement over exclamation. Numbers delivered gently. Humour comes from what is implied. No sarcasm tags, no memes, no pop-culture references, no swearing. Respect the taste rule in section 1.\n383\t\n384\t**Format:** at most 3 lines of 52 characters. Write at least 120 lines beyond the samples: every activity needs lines for 0/1/2/3★, first time and repeat; plus barks for ring entry and exit, falls and streaks.\n385\t\n386\t**Samples, in voice. Use them, then write more like them.**\n387\t\n388\t*Ounce:*\n389\t- \"Hello! I'm Ounce. Please step on me.\" / \"Ow.\" / \"That was a joke. I can't feel pain. I can only keep records.\"\n390\t- \"How old do you feel? This is not binding.\"\n391\t- \"Your Wobble Age is 68. Is that close? No? I'm so sorry.\"\n392\t- \"Thank you. I have written that down.\"\n393\t- \"You wobbled 14 times. I only counted the ones you noticed.\"\n394\t- \"Your left side is doing very well. I'll let your right side know.\"\n395\t- \"No change since yesterday. Which is, in a way, consistent.\"\n396\t- \"Excellent! ...Compared to Dennis.\"\n397\t- \"I'm not angry. Scales don't get angry. We get accurate.\"\n398\t- \"Have you been stretching? Please don't lie. I'm very sensitive.\"\n399\t- \"Today's concern: your ankles. I've been concerned all night.\"\n400\t- \"Good morning. You look rested. I can't see. But you felt rested.\"\n401\t- \"Kevin has been with us eleven years. He has never once held a pose.\"\n402\t- \"This is a recording. The person in it is doing better than you.\" *(attract mode)*\n403\t- \"I have been adding seven. To everyone. For years. It felt motivating.\"\n404\t- \"See you tomorrow. Bring your knees.\"\n405\t\n406\t*Coach Plumb:*\n407\t- \"You are a tree. A tree does not check its phone.\"\n408\t- \"Your left knee has wandered off. Please collect it.\"\n409\t- \"Breathe in. Not like that.\"\n410\t- \"Good. Again. That was also good. Again.\"\n411\t- \"Hold. You may blink on Thursday.\"\n412\t- \"I am eighty-one. I say this so that you feel something.\"\n413\t- \"Stillness is a muscle. So is regret. We train both here.\"\n414\t- \"The floor is your friend. It has never once let go.\"\n415\t\n416\t*Classmates:*\n417\t- Marguerite: \"Both hips, new. Knee, new. Opinions, original.\"\n418\t- Dennis: \"I used to do this professionally. Not this. Something near it.\"\n419\t- Dennis: \"It's fine. It's just the one leg.\"\n420\t- June: \"I'm pacing myself.\"\n421\t- June: \"My gran says you're doing your best. She said it very slowly.\"\n422\t\n423\t**Morning questions** (three answers; they change only the remark, and Ounce files them):\n424\t- When you stand up, what sound do you make? *Oof. / Hnng. / I have become the sound.*\n425\t- Have you ever apologised to a chair? *Yes. / Not yet. / It started it.*\n426\t- How many stairs is too many? *One. / All of them. / Depends who's watching.*\n427\t- How do you feel about your ankles? *Fine. / We don't speak. / Which ones?*\n428\t- What is your relationship with the floor? *Distant. / Improving. / It's complicated.*\n429\t- If your knees could talk, what would they say? *Please. / Why. / Nothing. They've given up.*\n430\t- Day 7: Are you happy? *Yes. / No. / Is this graded?* → \"It's all graded.\"\n431\t\n432\t---\n433\t\n434\t## 9. UI and UX: 10 feet, controller first\n435\t\n436\t**One UI for every device: the pixel HUD.** No DOM menus; same screens for pad, keyboard and mouse. Build a small kit in `src/ui/`.\n437\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"557126ca-6d30-481a-9998-d52917df8c4d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:12:39.676Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 6. Weigh-In and Wobble Age\n\nYour avatar steps onto Ounce (\"Ow.\" every time; the delivery varies). Close-up, huge dial, tiny animated needle.\n\n| Test | Rules (12-15 s) | Result T (0..1) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Stillness | Ring .30. Dot and ring fade after 3 s: \"Eyes closed.\" | in-ring fraction |\n| Lean | Three targets (\"70% left\"). Reach and hold ±.1 for 1.5 s each. | based on time |\n| Chase | Follow a slow target on a Lissajous path | 1 - mean distance × 2 |\n\nThen one question (section 8), then the reveal: the needle spins, the number rolls, Ounce remarks.\n\n```\ntrue  = round(20 + 60 × (1 - mean(last 3 T))) - min(20, totalStars × 0.5), clamped to 18..95\nshown = true + 7 until the confession, then true\n```\n\nThe chart draws 7 points. At the confession every point animates down by 7. Test it: an expert bot ends lower than an average one, an idle bot stays high, and the confession subtracts exactly 7.\n\n---\n\n## 7. The island hub\n\n`iso` camera ✔ (`{ preset: 'iso', zoom: 1.15 }`) with `PlatformerCharacter` and the kit's full moveset. Jumping and waving have no purpose and should still be there. Island about 44 × 34 m. The top of the screen is -x, -z: **put tall things in that quadrant** so they never hide the player.\n\n| Place | Near (x, z) | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| Weigh-In Terrace | (0, 3) | Day start, Ounce's dais |\n| Pavilion of Holding Still | (-11, 3), sky-blue roof | Poses |\n| The Rep Shed | (11, 3), orange roof | Reps |\n| Beat Beach | (12, -10), on sand | Hoop, Step |\n| Lagoon Games | (-12, -10), pier | Header, Slackline, Tray, Pier Jump |\n| Jogging Path gate | (0, 11) | Island Jog |\n| Sweat Jar | (4, -4) | Drips, milestones |\n| Locker Room | (-4, -4) | Avatar |\n| Hall of Numbers | (0, -8) | Records, chart, calendar |\n| Hammock between palms | (14, 10) | End the day |\n| Scenery | | Kettlebell Volcano (-15, -14), Foam Roller Hills (15, -14), Dumbbell Bridge over an inlet, medicine balls, gulls (`Boids`) overhead |\n\n- **Interaction:** a trigger shows `[✕] Enter: Pavilion of Holding Still`. Confirm opens a station menu: activities with stars and best score, locked rows greyed with the unlock day, one remark.\n- **Mouse:** hovering a station highlights it and names it; clicking walks there and enters; clicking ground walks there (pointer ray via `camera.rayAt`, then `castRay`). Steer the hero by writing its `MoveInput.move`.\n- **HUD:** day top-left, Drips top-right, today's prescription under the day, prompts bottom. Nothing else.\n- **Ounce** hops after you (`Squash`, tween) and barks at most every 6 s.\n- **Life:** classmates around the island doing small loops (stretching, sitting, failing).\n\n---\n\n## 8. Writing\n\n**Voice:** short declarative sentences. Polite, clinical, caring, faintly wounding. A remark should sound like it came from a nurse who has read your file. Understatement over exclamation. Numbers delivered gently. Humour comes from what is implied. No sarcasm tags, no memes, no pop-culture references, no swearing. Respect the taste rule in section 1.\n\n**Format:** at most 3 lines of 52 characters. Write at least 120 lines beyond the samples: every activity needs lines for 0/1/2/3★, first time and repeat; plus barks for ring entry and exit, falls and streaks.\n\n**Samples, in voice. Use them, then write more like them.**\n\n*Ounce:*\n- \"Hello! I'm Ounce. Please step on me.\" / \"Ow.\" / \"That was a joke. I can't feel pain. I can only keep records.\"\n- \"How old do you feel? This is not binding.\"\n- \"Your Wobble Age is 68. Is that close? No? I'm so sorry.\"\n- \"Thank you. I have written that down.\"\n- \"You wobbled 14 times. I only counted the ones you noticed.\"\n- \"Your left side is doing very well. I'll let your right side know.\"\n- \"No change since yesterday. Which is, in a way, consistent.\"\n- \"Excellent! ...Compared to Dennis.\"\n- \"I'm not angry. Scales don't get angry. We get accurate.\"\n- \"Have you been stretching? Please don't lie. I'm very sensitive.\"\n- \"Today's concern: your ankles. I've been concerned all night.\"\n- \"Good morning. You look rested. I can't see. But you felt rested.\"\n- \"Kevin has been with us eleven years. He has never once held a pose.\"\n- \"This is a recording. The person in it is doing better than you.\" *(attract mode)*\n- \"I have been adding seven. To everyone. For years. It felt motivating.\"\n- \"See you tomorrow. Bring your knees.\"\n\n*Coach Plumb:*\n- \"You are a tree. A tree does not check its phone.\"\n- \"Your left knee has wandered off. Please collect it.\"\n- \"Breathe in. Not like that.\"\n- \"Good. Again. That was also good. Again.\"\n- \"Hold. You may blink on Thursday.\"\n- \"I am eighty-one. I say this so that you feel something.\"\n- \"Stillness is a muscle. So is regret. We train both here.\"\n- \"The floor is your friend. It has never once let go.\"\n\n*Classmates:*\n- Marguerite: \"Both hips, new. Knee, new. Opinions, original.\"\n- Dennis: \"I used to do this professionally. Not this. Something near it.\"\n- Dennis: \"It's fine. It's just the one leg.\"\n- June: \"I'm pacing myself.\"\n- June: \"My gran says you're doing your best. She said it very slowly.\"\n\n**Morning questions** (three answers; they change only the remark, and Ounce files them):\n- When you stand up, what sound do you make? *Oof. / Hnng. / I have become the sound.*\n- Have you ever apologised to a chair? *Yes. / Not yet. / It started it.*\n- How many stairs is too many? *One. / All of them. / Depends who's watching.*\n- How do you feel about your ankles? *Fine. / We don't speak. / Which ones?*\n- What is your relationship with the floor? *Distant. / Improving. / It's complicated.*\n- If your knees could talk, what would they say? *Please. / Why. / Nothing. They've given up.*\n- Day 7: Are you happy? *Yes. / No. / Is this graded?* → \"It's all graded.\"\n\n---\n\n## 9. UI and UX: 10 feet, controller first\n\n**One UI for every device: the pixel HUD.** No DOM menus; same screens for pad, keyboard and mouse. Build a small kit in `src/ui/`.\n","numLines":105,"startLine":333,"totalLines":993}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FxkjzAuStMmQzuARnJCKxL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
