{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjbvuiDc57Gf72aiJXoq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VVN2Vk9W7MGwStaLJi98aN","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","offset":572,"limit":100},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9803,"cache_read_input_tokens":369151,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9803},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"55821f88-a5a7-4ccf-9b25-3a64dd838ded","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:13:27.136Z","request_id":"req_011CgjbvuMtZ1uL9QHskdnZZ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VVN2Vk9W7MGwStaLJi98aN":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","offset":572,"limit":100}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VVN2Vk9W7MGwStaLJi98aN","type":"tool_result","content":"572\t<script>/* session.js pasted unmodified: first script, right after charset */</script>\n573\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n574\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n575\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n576\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most across three events. Stay in the circle.\">\n577\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J: step.\">\n578\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">\n579\t<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n580\t```\n581\t\n582\tBoot order ✔:\n583\t\n584\t```js\n585\tlet info = null;\n586\tif (window.AIHub?.active) info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n587\tconst engine = await Engine.start(firstScene, withUrlOptions({ /* ... */ seed: info ? info.seed : savedOrDefaultSeed }));\n588\tif (info) AIHub.ready();                 // no key press, as soon as the card can show\n589\t```\n590\t\n591\tIf `connect()` answers null, carry on as the normal game. Without WebGPU, `Engine.start` rejects and the engine prints \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable: ...\" on the page ✔. Catch the rejection, or it also surfaces as a page error ✔, and call `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\n592\t\n593\t**In a session:**\n594\t- **The card (`card: true`)** is the game's own: the players' avatars lining up on mats in seat colours (`#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`), {TITLE}, ready ticks, how to win, the controls for the last device, the time left from the `card` event. Enter or Cross → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; Triangle or M → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Use a **direct `keydown` listener for Enter** ✔ here. No menus. Cosmetic randomness only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n595\t- **Start:** on `start` show a countdown from `AIHub.time()`; play at `time() >= 0`. Event windows are read from `AIHub.time()`, so all copies stay in step.\n596\t- **Same world:** gusts, pose picks and object waves come from `AIHub.rng(label)` or the seeded `ctx.random`.\n597\t- **Ghosts:** a `setInterval` at 100 ms (not tied to rendering) sends `AIHub.send({ a: eventIndex, x, y, c: clipIndex, t: clipTime, s: score }, { reliable: false })` and calls `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`. Start as soon as `start` arrives, even with score 0: the harness needs both within seconds. Receivers lerp the other mats; they never simulate them, and they hide a ghost whose `a` differs from theirs.\n598\t- **`leave`:** that avatar waves and walks off. The round goes on, host included.\n599\t- **End:** `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once, at the end of the Medley or at once on `time-up`. On `end`: stop input, stop sound, send nothing.\n600\t- **Never:** no title, attract, dev mode, saves, quit or restart; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `window.open` or navigation. Names come from `info.players` and are drawn with `say()`.\n601\t\n602\t---\n603\t\n604\t## 13. Art direction\n605\t\n606\t**Base: the engine's native look**, default pixel pipeline, toon materials, 16-colour palette (`look` left unset). The scene reads clean and bright: white, mist, sky and cyan, with lime and sand for growth and warmth, orange and red as accents. Start with `quality: 'high'` (`'medium'` in sessions, where several copies may share a machine in testing).\n607\t\n608\t**Performance is out of scope.** Add the detail the scene wants and don't spend time on optimisation.\n609\t\n610\t### Avatars ✔\n611\t\n612\tRe-dress the kit's hero with the same rig. This is proven to look good at gameplay framing: egg heads, dot eyes, hair caps. Use `castShadow: false` plus `ContactShadow` ✔: casting on the model gave ugly self-shadow blotches. The hero's `Eyes` mesh reads as sunglasses, so hide it. Compile clips once and share them between avatars.\n613\t\n614\t```js\n615\tfunction soften(mesh, kind = 'prism') { // same bounding box, softer shape\n616\t  mesh.geometry.computeBoundingBox();\n617\t  const b = mesh.geometry.boundingBox, s = b.getSize(new Vector3()), c = b.getCenter(new Vector3());\n618\t  const g = kind === 'egg' ? new SphereGeometry(0.5, 10, 8) : new CylinderGeometry(0.5, 0.5, 1, 8);\n619\t  g.scale(s.x, s.y, s.z); g.translate(c.x, c.y, c.z); mesh.geometry = g;\n620\t}\n621\texport function dress(root, look) { // look: { skin, top, bottom, shoe, hair, long?, bun?, headband? } as palette names\n622\t  const hide = new Set(['Moustache', 'ButtonR', 'ButtonL', 'Hat', 'Brim', 'Eyes', 'Nose']);\n623\t  const SLOT = { Overalls: 'bottom', ThighR: 'bottom', ThighL: 'bottom', ShinR_Mesh: look.long ? 'bottom' : 'skin', ShinL_Mesh: look.long ? 'bottom' : 'skin',\n624\t    Shirt: 'top', SleeveR: 'top', SleeveL: 'top', ForearmR_Mesh: look.long ? 'top' : 'skin', ForearmL_Mesh: look.long ? 'top' : 'skin',\n625\t    GloveR: 'skin', GloveL: 'skin', Face: 'skin', ShoeR: 'shoe', ShoeL: 'shoe' };\n626\t  root.traverse((o) => {\n627\t    if (!o.isMesh) return;\n628\t    if (hide.has(o.name)) { o.visible = false; return; }\n629\t    if (SLOT[o.name]) o.material = toonMaterial(PALETTE[look[SLOT[o.name]]]);\n630\t    if (o.name === 'Face') soften(o, 'egg'); else if (/Sleeve|Forearm|Thigh|Shin|Glove/.test(o.name)) soften(o);\n631\t  });\n632\t  const face = root.getObjectByName('Face'); face.geometry.computeBoundingBox();\n633\t  const fb = face.geometry.boundingBox, size = fb.getSize(new Vector3()), c = fb.getCenter(new Vector3());\n634\t  const add = (m, x, y, z) => { m.position.set(x, y, z); face.parent.add(m); return m; };\n635\t  for (const sx of [-1, 1]) add(new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.055, 0.09, 0.03), toonMaterial(PALETTE.ink)), c.x + sx * size.x * 0.2, c.y + 0.02, c.z + size.z * 0.48);\n636\t  add(new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.1, 0.022, 0.03), toonMaterial(PALETTE.ink)), c.x, c.y - size.y * 0.2, c.z + size.z * 0.47);\n637\t  const hair = add(new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(0.5, 10, 6, 0, Math.PI * 2, 0, Math.PI * 0.55), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.hair])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.04, c.z - size.z * 0.05);\n638\t  hair.scale.set(size.x * 1.08, size.y * 1.04, size.z * 1.08);\n639\t  if (look.bun) add(new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(0.1, 8, 6), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.hair])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.6, c.z - size.z * 0.2);\n640\t  if (look.headband) { const b2 = add(new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.5, 0.5, 1, 10), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.headband])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.16, c.z); b2.scale.set(size.x * 1.06, 0.06, size.z * 1.06); }\n641\t}\n642\t```\n643\t\n644\tAdd more hair shapes as extra meshes on the head. Good casting: player `{ skin:'sand', top:'white', bottom:'sky', shoe:'white', hair:'ink', headband:'red' }`; Coach `{ skin:'sand', top:'cyan', bottom:'cyan', shoe:'white', hair:'mist', bun:true, long:true }`, plus a plumb bob on a string (`SpringChain`) from her wrist.\n645\t\n646\t### Ounce ✔ (zero problems, zero warnings on the model sheet)\n647\t\n648\t```js\n649\texport const ounce = model({\n650\t  id: 'ounce', about: 'Ounce: a mint retro bathroom scale whose round dial is its face', tags: ['character'], size: [1.1, 1.05, 1.1],\n651\t  palette: { body: 'cyan', base: 'teal', tread: 'sky', face: 'white', rim: 'slate', tick: 'mist', needle: 'red', eye: 'ink' },\n652\t  parts: [\n653\t    { name: 'base', box: [1.04, 0.08, 1.04], at: [0, 0.04, 0], c: 'base' },\n654\t    { name: 'plate', box: [0.96, 0.2, 0.96], at: [0, 0.18, 0], c: 'body' },\n655\t    { mirror: [{ name: 'tread', box: [0.3, 0.03, 0.42], at: [0.22, 0.295, -0.22], c: 'tread' }], axis: 'x' },\n656\t    { group: [\n657\t        { name: 'neck', box: [0.5, 0.42, 0.14], at: [0, 0.21, 0], c: 'body' },\n658\t        { group: [\n659\t            { name: 'rim', cyl: [0.78, 0.1, 0.78], at: [0, 0, 0], c: 'rim', seg: 14 },\n660\t            { name: 'dial', cyl: [0.66, 0.04, 0.66], at: [0, 0.06, 0], c: 'face', seg: 14 },\n661\t            ...[-60, -30, 0, 30, 60].map((a) => ({ box: [0.06, 0.03, 0.09], at: [Math.sin(a * Math.PI / 180) * 0.26, 0.085, -Math.cos(a * Math.PI / 180) * 0.26], rot: [0, -a, 0], c: 'tick' })),\n662\t            { mirror: [{ name: 'eye', box: [0.08, 0.03, 0.11], at: [0.12, 0.09, -0.07], c: 'eye' }], axis: 'x' },\n663\t            { group: [{ name: 'needleBar', box: [0.06, 0.03, 0.22], at: [0, 0, 0.1], c: 'needle' }, { name: 'hub', cyl: [0.07, 0.04, 0.07], at: [0, 0, 0], c: 'needle', seg: 8 }], name: 'needle', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.1, 0.1], rot: [0, 180, 0] },\n664\t          ], name: 'face', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.5, 0.08], rot: [72, 0, 0] },\n665\t      ], name: 'head', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.26, 0.2] },\n666\t  ],\n667\t});\n668\t```\n669\t\n670\tPivots stay movable: `build.object.getObjectByName('needle')` for mood, `'face'` for nods. Scale Ounce ×1.4 on the island and frame close in Weigh-In. Squash on hops.\n671\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"dc137666-4a87-410d-a9d5-83c705d7c8c3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:13:27.145Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","content":"<script>/* session.js pasted unmodified: first script, right after charset */</script>\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most across three events. Stay in the circle.\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J: step.\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n```\n\nBoot order ✔:\n\n```js\nlet info = null;\nif (window.AIHub?.active) info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\nconst engine = await Engine.start(firstScene, withUrlOptions({ /* ... */ seed: info ? info.seed : savedOrDefaultSeed }));\nif (info) AIHub.ready();                 // no key press, as soon as the card can show\n```\n\nIf `connect()` answers null, carry on as the normal game. Without WebGPU, `Engine.start` rejects and the engine prints \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable: ...\" on the page ✔. Catch the rejection, or it also surfaces as a page error ✔, and call `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\n\n**In a session:**\n- **The card (`card: true`)** is the game's own: the players' avatars lining up on mats in seat colours (`#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`), {TITLE}, ready ticks, how to win, the controls for the last device, the time left from the `card` event. Enter or Cross → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; Triangle or M → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Use a **direct `keydown` listener for Enter** ✔ here. No menus. Cosmetic randomness only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n- **Start:** on `start` show a countdown from `AIHub.time()`; play at `time() >= 0`. Event windows are read from `AIHub.time()`, so all copies stay in step.\n- **Same world:** gusts, pose picks and object waves come from `AIHub.rng(label)` or the seeded `ctx.random`.\n- **Ghosts:** a `setInterval` at 100 ms (not tied to rendering) sends `AIHub.send({ a: eventIndex, x, y, c: clipIndex, t: clipTime, s: score }, { reliable: false })` and calls `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`. Start as soon as `start` arrives, even with score 0: the harness needs both within seconds. Receivers lerp the other mats; they never simulate them, and they hide a ghost whose `a` differs from theirs.\n- **`leave`:** that avatar waves and walks off. The round goes on, host included.\n- **End:** `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once, at the end of the Medley or at once on `time-up`. On `end`: stop input, stop sound, send nothing.\n- **Never:** no title, attract, dev mode, saves, quit or restart; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `window.open` or navigation. Names come from `info.players` and are drawn with `say()`.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Art direction\n\n**Base: the engine's native look**, default pixel pipeline, toon materials, 16-colour palette (`look` left unset). The scene reads clean and bright: white, mist, sky and cyan, with lime and sand for growth and warmth, orange and red as accents. Start with `quality: 'high'` (`'medium'` in sessions, where several copies may share a machine in testing).\n\n**Performance is out of scope.** Add the detail the scene wants and don't spend time on optimisation.\n\n### Avatars ✔\n\nRe-dress the kit's hero with the same rig. This is proven to look good at gameplay framing: egg heads, dot eyes, hair caps. Use `castShadow: false` plus `ContactShadow` ✔: casting on the model gave ugly self-shadow blotches. The hero's `Eyes` mesh reads as sunglasses, so hide it. Compile clips once and share them between avatars.\n\n```js\nfunction soften(mesh, kind = 'prism') { // same bounding box, softer shape\n  mesh.geometry.computeBoundingBox();\n  const b = mesh.geometry.boundingBox, s = b.getSize(new Vector3()), c = b.getCenter(new Vector3());\n  const g = kind === 'egg' ? new SphereGeometry(0.5, 10, 8) : new CylinderGeometry(0.5, 0.5, 1, 8);\n  g.scale(s.x, s.y, s.z); g.translate(c.x, c.y, c.z); mesh.geometry = g;\n}\nexport function dress(root, look) { // look: { skin, top, bottom, shoe, hair, long?, bun?, headband? } as palette names\n  const hide = new Set(['Moustache', 'ButtonR', 'ButtonL', 'Hat', 'Brim', 'Eyes', 'Nose']);\n  const SLOT = { Overalls: 'bottom', ThighR: 'bottom', ThighL: 'bottom', ShinR_Mesh: look.long ? 'bottom' : 'skin', ShinL_Mesh: look.long ? 'bottom' : 'skin',\n    Shirt: 'top', SleeveR: 'top', SleeveL: 'top', ForearmR_Mesh: look.long ? 'top' : 'skin', ForearmL_Mesh: look.long ? 'top' : 'skin',\n    GloveR: 'skin', GloveL: 'skin', Face: 'skin', ShoeR: 'shoe', ShoeL: 'shoe' };\n  root.traverse((o) => {\n    if (!o.isMesh) return;\n    if (hide.has(o.name)) { o.visible = false; return; }\n    if (SLOT[o.name]) o.material = toonMaterial(PALETTE[look[SLOT[o.name]]]);\n    if (o.name === 'Face') soften(o, 'egg'); else if (/Sleeve|Forearm|Thigh|Shin|Glove/.test(o.name)) soften(o);\n  });\n  const face = root.getObjectByName('Face'); face.geometry.computeBoundingBox();\n  const fb = face.geometry.boundingBox, size = fb.getSize(new Vector3()), c = fb.getCenter(new Vector3());\n  const add = (m, x, y, z) => { m.position.set(x, y, z); face.parent.add(m); return m; };\n  for (const sx of [-1, 1]) add(new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.055, 0.09, 0.03), toonMaterial(PALETTE.ink)), c.x + sx * size.x * 0.2, c.y + 0.02, c.z + size.z * 0.48);\n  add(new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.1, 0.022, 0.03), toonMaterial(PALETTE.ink)), c.x, c.y - size.y * 0.2, c.z + size.z * 0.47);\n  const hair = add(new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(0.5, 10, 6, 0, Math.PI * 2, 0, Math.PI * 0.55), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.hair])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.04, c.z - size.z * 0.05);\n  hair.scale.set(size.x * 1.08, size.y * 1.04, size.z * 1.08);\n  if (look.bun) add(new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(0.1, 8, 6), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.hair])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.6, c.z - size.z * 0.2);\n  if (look.headband) { const b2 = add(new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.5, 0.5, 1, 10), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.headband])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.16, c.z); b2.scale.set(size.x * 1.06, 0.06, size.z * 1.06); }\n}\n```\n\nAdd more hair shapes as extra meshes on the head. Good casting: player `{ skin:'sand', top:'white', bottom:'sky', shoe:'white', hair:'ink', headband:'red' }`; Coach `{ skin:'sand', top:'cyan', bottom:'cyan', shoe:'white', hair:'mist', bun:true, long:true }`, plus a plumb bob on a string (`SpringChain`) from her wrist.\n\n### Ounce ✔ (zero problems, zero warnings on the model sheet)\n\n```js\nexport const ounce = model({\n  id: 'ounce', about: 'Ounce: a mint retro bathroom scale whose round dial is its face', tags: ['character'], size: [1.1, 1.05, 1.1],\n  palette: { body: 'cyan', base: 'teal', tread: 'sky', face: 'white', rim: 'slate', tick: 'mist', needle: 'red', eye: 'ink' },\n  parts: [\n    { name: 'base', box: [1.04, 0.08, 1.04], at: [0, 0.04, 0], c: 'base' },\n    { name: 'plate', box: [0.96, 0.2, 0.96], at: [0, 0.18, 0], c: 'body' },\n    { mirror: [{ name: 'tread', box: [0.3, 0.03, 0.42], at: [0.22, 0.295, -0.22], c: 'tread' }], axis: 'x' },\n    { group: [\n        { name: 'neck', box: [0.5, 0.42, 0.14], at: [0, 0.21, 0], c: 'body' },\n        { group: [\n            { name: 'rim', cyl: [0.78, 0.1, 0.78], at: [0, 0, 0], c: 'rim', seg: 14 },\n            { name: 'dial', cyl: [0.66, 0.04, 0.66], at: [0, 0.06, 0], c: 'face', seg: 14 },\n            ...[-60, -30, 0, 30, 60].map((a) => ({ box: [0.06, 0.03, 0.09], at: [Math.sin(a * Math.PI / 180) * 0.26, 0.085, -Math.cos(a * Math.PI / 180) * 0.26], rot: [0, -a, 0], c: 'tick' })),\n            { mirror: [{ name: 'eye', box: [0.08, 0.03, 0.11], at: [0.12, 0.09, -0.07], c: 'eye' }], axis: 'x' },\n            { group: [{ name: 'needleBar', box: [0.06, 0.03, 0.22], at: [0, 0, 0.1], c: 'needle' }, { name: 'hub', cyl: [0.07, 0.04, 0.07], at: [0, 0, 0], c: 'needle', seg: 8 }], name: 'needle', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.1, 0.1], rot: [0, 180, 0] },\n          ], name: 'face', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.5, 0.08], rot: [72, 0, 0] },\n      ], name: 'head', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.26, 0.2] },\n  ],\n});\n```\n\nPivots stay movable: `build.object.getObjectByName('needle')` for mood, `'face'` for nods. Scale Ounce ×1.4 on the island and frame close in Weigh-In. Squash on hops.\n","numLines":100,"startLine":572,"totalLines":993}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VVN2Vk9W7MGwStaLJi98aN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
