{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjbyQPh7GXNTNwdXyE5U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pb7JwcKyiTqAQXc4xkxctg","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","offset":672,"limit":90},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11434,"cache_read_input_tokens":378954,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11434},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"71e794f8-a8a1-4e79-afec-c762f0278ff0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:13:36.306Z","request_id":"req_011CgjbyPnjV8bhFejU2huxo","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Pb7JwcKyiTqAQXc4xkxctg":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","offset":672,"limit":90}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pb7JwcKyiTqAQXc4xkxctg","type":"tool_result","content":"672\t### Models to write as data (`src/art/models.js`; check each with `node check.mjs --sheets src/art/models.js`)\n673\t\n674\tKettlebell Volcano ✔ (`ball [12,9,12]`, `torus` handle, glowing top), Foam Roller Hill ✔ (a big `cyl` on its side with bands), Dumbbell Bridge ✔, medicine ball ✔, Pavilion ✔ (columns, `cone` roof, recolour per station), Sweat Jar ✔ (`{ lathe: [[.85,0],[.95,.1],[.95,2.1],[.75,2.4],[.75,2.55]], at: [0,.3,0], seg: 12 }` for the glass, plus plinth, lid and label; **toon materials are opaque, so fake the fluid**: a `sky` cylinder 1 cm wider than the wall, scaled in y with Drips, with a white highlight stripe), Rep Shed, Beat Stage with speakers, pier with railings, palm (`tube` trunk, fronds; the library has none), yoga mat, step platform, hoop (`torus`), coconut, flip-flop, golden pineapple, catapult, tray and cups, vitamin, slackline anchors, hammock, lockers, Hall of Numbers board, judges' paddles, mobility scooter, ferry, water cup, sprinkler, Kevin (body, wings, feet, with a two-pose flap).\n675\t\n676\tFrom the library, generic props are fine: `fountain`, `bench`, `lamp-post`, `bush`, `flowers`, `oak`, `fence`, `signpost`, `table`.\n677\t\n678\t### Surfaces and scene effects\n679\t\n680\t- **Tile floor ✔:** `textureDef({ id:'clinic-tile', size:[16,16], tile:true, palette:{ grout:'mist', a:'white', b:'white' }, layers:[{ pattern:'tiles', colors:['grout','a','b'], w:16, h:16, mortar:1, seed:3 }], about:'...', tags:['floor'] })`, added to `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`. **Never stretch a map over a box ✔** (it gave one giant tile): use a `PlaneGeometry` and scale its UVs by metres ÷ (16 / `DEFAULT_TEXEL`), as the kit's market example does.\n681\t- **World:** `WaterSurface` ✔, `GrassField` ✔, sand and lawn as flat boxes ✔, `RippleField` at splashes, `Precipitation` in the finale, `Boids` gulls, `Decals` footprints on sand.\n682\t- **Light:** `ctx.lights` for pavilion lanterns at dusk; `applySky(skyAt(h))` for morning and evening.\n683\t- **Game feel:** `hitstop`, `shake`, `screen.flash`, `screen.shockwave` on the splash, iris transitions (`screen.cover`/`reveal` ✔, also resolve headless), `Trail` behind the jogger, custom particles ('sweat' in cyan, 'confetti', 'splash', 'zen' motes).\n684\t- **Cutscenes:** ferry arrival, confession and ending with `Timeline` ✔. On the `fixed` preset, apply `tl.camera()` each frame to `ctx.camera.camera` (position, `lookAt`, fov, `updateProjectionMatrix`) ✔. Use `tl.line()` for subtitles, `tl.bars()` for letterbox.\n685\t\n686\t---\n687\t\n688\t## 14. Animation\n689\t\n690\tUse the engine's native system: `ClipDef` data, `compileClips`, `THREE.AnimationMixer` for class avatars, `PlatformerCharacter` on the island, procedural layers (`Squash`, `SpringChain`) for character.\n691\t\n692\t**Conventions** (`HERO_RIG`): facing +Z. Arm X: -90 ahead, -180 overhead. Arm Z: out to the side (R negative, L positive). Forearm -X bends the elbow. Leg -X swings forward. Shin +X bends the knee. Foot +X points the toes. Pelvis `p` offsets, `r` tips the whole body. Torso +X bends forward.\n693\t\n694\t**Verified poses ✔** (`validateClip` clean, `analyzeClip` no problems, reviewed on contact sheets):\n695\t\n696\t```js\n697\tconst hold = (name, pose) => ({ name, frames: 60, loop: true, keys: [[0, pose], [60, pose]] });\n698\tconst feet = (pose, R, L) => placeFeet(pose, HERO_RIG, { R, L });\n699\thold('Tree', { Pelvis: { p: [0.03, -0.02, 0] }, ArmR: [-172, 0, -6], ForearmR: [-14, 0, 0], ArmL: [-172, 0, 6], ForearmL: [-14, 0, 0], LegR: [-62, 0, -58], ShinR: [150, 0, 0], FootR: [30, 0, 0] });\n700\thold('Heron', { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.02, 0] }, Torso: [10, 0, 0], Head: [-14, 0, 0], ArmR: [-20, 0, -80], ArmL: [-20, 0, 80], ForearmR: [-30, 0, 0], ForearmL: [-30, 0, 0], LegR: [-85, 0, 0], ShinR: [95, 0, 0], FootR: [35, 0, 0] });\n701\thold('Warrior', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.2, 0] }, Torso: [0, 25, 0], Head: [0, 40, 0], ArmR: [0, 0, -90], ArmL: [0, 0, 90] }, { z: 0.38 }, { z: -0.38 }));\n702\thold('Chair', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.28, -0.06] }, Torso: [24, 0, 0], Head: [-18, 0, 0], ArmR: [-110, 0, -8], ArmL: [-110, 0, 8] }, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 }));\n703\thold('Fold', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.03, -0.03] }, Torso: [88, 0, 0], Head: [10, 0, 0], ArmR: [-70, 0, -6], ArmL: [-70, 0, 6], ForearmR: [-8, 0, 0], ForearmL: [-8, 0, 0] }, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 }));\n704\thold('Plank', { Pelvis: { r: [66, 0, 0], p: [0, -0.2, 0] }, Head: [-48, 0, 0], ArmR: [-63, 0, -5], ArmL: [-63, 0, 5], HandR: [-40, 0, 0], HandL: [-40, 0, 0], FootR: [55, 0, 0], FootL: [55, 0, 0] });\n705\t// Scrubbed reps: keys built with placeFeet AND a feet track, or the sole dips through the floor mid-clip.\n706\tconst squatTop = { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.02, 0] }, Torso: [2, 0, 0], ArmR: [6, 0, -9], ArmL: [6, 0, 9] }, squatLow = { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.3, -0.05] }, Torso: [26, 0, 0], Head: [-20, 0, 0], ArmR: [-85, 0, -8], ArmL: [-85, 0, 8] };\n707\t({ name: 'SquatRep', frames: 30, grounded: true, keys: [[0, feet(squatTop, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 })], [30, feet(squatLow, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 })]], feet: [[0, { R: { z: 0 }, L: { z: 0 } }], [30, { R: { z: 0 }, L: { z: 0 } }]] });\n708\t// LungeRep: the same way, low pose Pelvis p [0,-0.24,0], Torso [6,0,0], goals R { z: .34 }, L { z: -.32, pitch: 25, pivot: 'ball' }. For the left side, map poses through mirror(pose, HERO_RIG) and swap R and L goals.\n709\t```\n710\t\n711\t**Still to author:** Press; StepL/StepR; header nod; flail; daze; bow; slow clap; sneeze; Coach's point and demonstration transitions; tuck and cannonball; judge raising a paddle; stepping onto Ounce; ferry disembark. Reuse kit clips: `Idle`, `Walk`, `Run`, `Sit`, `LieIdle`, `Wave`, `Victory`, `Teeter`, `Hurt`, `Fall`, `GetUp`, and more (`HERO_CLIPS`).\n712\t\n713\t**Preview without a GPU ✔:** `tools/clip-sheet.mjs` uses `renderSheet(model, HERO_RIG, def, clip, { frames, views: ['front', 'side'], scale: 90, trails: false, skeleton: false })` → `{ width, height, data }`, written as a PNG with `node:zlib` (`deflateSync`, `crc32`). Look at every new pose once. Hide the hat and moustache first so you judge the real silhouette.\n714\t\n715\t---\n716\t\n717\t## 15. Audio\n718\t\n719\tEverything is written in code. No audio files.\n720\t\n721\t### Music\n722\t\n723\t- **`ctx.audio.setVolume('music', savedMusic ?? 0.10)` at boot, every boot**, from your own settings key. The engine's default is 60%, and its stored volume key (`pixel-engine:audio`) is shared by every engine game on the origin, so don't rely on it.\n724\t- **Write instruments loud:** track `volume` 0.45-0.8. The kit's examples use about 0.12, written for a 60% bus; at 10% × master .8 that is near silence. A test checks each song: sum of track volumes × 0.1 × 0.8 ≥ 0.03.\n725\t- Songs are `Song` data, in `src/audio/songs.js`, each original, none imitating the source:\n726\t\n727\t| Song | Feel |\n728\t|---|---|\n729\t| Title / Plaza | gentle waiting-room bossa, about 92 BPM, soft triangle plucks |\n730\t| Holding Still | slow, sparse, breath-paced, 60 BPM |\n731\t| Rep Shed | light funk bass, 110 BPM |\n732\t| Beat Beach (Hoop) and Step Class | bright, four-on-the-floor; Step is 104 BPM exactly |\n733\t| Lagoon Games | staccato ukulele feel, 120 BPM |\n734\t| Jog | steady, cheerful, 112 BPM |\n735\t| Evening Report | music box, 70 BPM |\n736\t| Long Stand | near silence, then one swelling chord line at t = 75 |\n737\t\n738\t### SFX\n739\t\n740\t`ctx.audio.register` data: needle tick, ring chime in/out, wobble warning, rep tick, step perfect/good, combo, coconut bonk, flip-flop thwap, hoop whirr (`loop`), splash, gust, gull squawk, jar drip, star pop, menu move/confirm/back, \"Ow\" stinger.\n741\t\n742\t### Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish\n743\t\n744\tBuild in `src/audio/voice.js`:\n745\t\n746\t1. **`syllabify(text, speaker)` is pure and testable in Node.** Words split into syllables; a hash of each word picks consonant class and vowel, so **the same word always sounds the same**. Output: `[{ t, dur, f0, vowel, cons, charIndex }]`. Declination -15% across a sentence; `?` rises 25% at the end; `!` +15%; `...` slows. The dialogue typewriter reads `charIndex`.\n747\t2. **`renderVoice(ctx, destination, syllables, when)`** schedules, per syllable: a saw oscillator at `f0` through two parallel bandpass filters at the vowel's formants (a 800/1200, e 500/1900, i 300/2300, o 500/900, u 350/800, × speaker shift), gain envelope 6 ms up, 30 ms down; a noise burst for plosives (8 ms) and fricatives (40 ms).\n748\t3. **Routing:** it works on any `BaseAudioContext`, so it renders in `OfflineAudioContext` for tests. Live, use `ctx.audio.context`, connected to `ctx.audio.buses.sfx` (undocumented but present in 0.46.0, so master and mute apply) via your own Voice gain. `ctx.audio.context` is null headless and before the first input: no-op and log.\n749\t\n750\t| Speaker | f0 | Syllables/s | Formant shift | Extra |\n751\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n752\t| Ounce | 340 | 13 | ×1.25 | a needle tick on punctuation |\n753\t| Coach | 165 | 7.5 | ×.9 | flat pitch, long pauses |\n754\t| Marguerite | 230 | 9 | ×1 | slight vibrato |\n755\t| Dennis | 120 | 11 | ×.95 | pitch up on last word |\n756\t| June | 300 | 10 | ×1.15 | no contour at all |\n757\t| Kevin | | | | squawk SFX, never words |\n758\t\n759\t---\n760\t\n761\t## 16. Architecture"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"34bbc31d-a555-4157-9806-b2b64373455a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:13:36.325Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-230741__x6981e3/work/PLAN.md","content":"### Models to write as data (`src/art/models.js`; check each with `node check.mjs --sheets src/art/models.js`)\n\nKettlebell Volcano ✔ (`ball [12,9,12]`, `torus` handle, glowing top), Foam Roller Hill ✔ (a big `cyl` on its side with bands), Dumbbell Bridge ✔, medicine ball ✔, Pavilion ✔ (columns, `cone` roof, recolour per station), Sweat Jar ✔ (`{ lathe: [[.85,0],[.95,.1],[.95,2.1],[.75,2.4],[.75,2.55]], at: [0,.3,0], seg: 12 }` for the glass, plus plinth, lid and label; **toon materials are opaque, so fake the fluid**: a `sky` cylinder 1 cm wider than the wall, scaled in y with Drips, with a white highlight stripe), Rep Shed, Beat Stage with speakers, pier with railings, palm (`tube` trunk, fronds; the library has none), yoga mat, step platform, hoop (`torus`), coconut, flip-flop, golden pineapple, catapult, tray and cups, vitamin, slackline anchors, hammock, lockers, Hall of Numbers board, judges' paddles, mobility scooter, ferry, water cup, sprinkler, Kevin (body, wings, feet, with a two-pose flap).\n\nFrom the library, generic props are fine: `fountain`, `bench`, `lamp-post`, `bush`, `flowers`, `oak`, `fence`, `signpost`, `table`.\n\n### Surfaces and scene effects\n\n- **Tile floor ✔:** `textureDef({ id:'clinic-tile', size:[16,16], tile:true, palette:{ grout:'mist', a:'white', b:'white' }, layers:[{ pattern:'tiles', colors:['grout','a','b'], w:16, h:16, mortar:1, seed:3 }], about:'...', tags:['floor'] })`, added to `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`. **Never stretch a map over a box ✔** (it gave one giant tile): use a `PlaneGeometry` and scale its UVs by metres ÷ (16 / `DEFAULT_TEXEL`), as the kit's market example does.\n- **World:** `WaterSurface` ✔, `GrassField` ✔, sand and lawn as flat boxes ✔, `RippleField` at splashes, `Precipitation` in the finale, `Boids` gulls, `Decals` footprints on sand.\n- **Light:** `ctx.lights` for pavilion lanterns at dusk; `applySky(skyAt(h))` for morning and evening.\n- **Game feel:** `hitstop`, `shake`, `screen.flash`, `screen.shockwave` on the splash, iris transitions (`screen.cover`/`reveal` ✔, also resolve headless), `Trail` behind the jogger, custom particles ('sweat' in cyan, 'confetti', 'splash', 'zen' motes).\n- **Cutscenes:** ferry arrival, confession and ending with `Timeline` ✔. On the `fixed` preset, apply `tl.camera()` each frame to `ctx.camera.camera` (position, `lookAt`, fov, `updateProjectionMatrix`) ✔. Use `tl.line()` for subtitles, `tl.bars()` for letterbox.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Animation\n\nUse the engine's native system: `ClipDef` data, `compileClips`, `THREE.AnimationMixer` for class avatars, `PlatformerCharacter` on the island, procedural layers (`Squash`, `SpringChain`) for character.\n\n**Conventions** (`HERO_RIG`): facing +Z. Arm X: -90 ahead, -180 overhead. Arm Z: out to the side (R negative, L positive). Forearm -X bends the elbow. Leg -X swings forward. Shin +X bends the knee. Foot +X points the toes. Pelvis `p` offsets, `r` tips the whole body. Torso +X bends forward.\n\n**Verified poses ✔** (`validateClip` clean, `analyzeClip` no problems, reviewed on contact sheets):\n\n```js\nconst hold = (name, pose) => ({ name, frames: 60, loop: true, keys: [[0, pose], [60, pose]] });\nconst feet = (pose, R, L) => placeFeet(pose, HERO_RIG, { R, L });\nhold('Tree', { Pelvis: { p: [0.03, -0.02, 0] }, ArmR: [-172, 0, -6], ForearmR: [-14, 0, 0], ArmL: [-172, 0, 6], ForearmL: [-14, 0, 0], LegR: [-62, 0, -58], ShinR: [150, 0, 0], FootR: [30, 0, 0] });\nhold('Heron', { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.02, 0] }, Torso: [10, 0, 0], Head: [-14, 0, 0], ArmR: [-20, 0, -80], ArmL: [-20, 0, 80], ForearmR: [-30, 0, 0], ForearmL: [-30, 0, 0], LegR: [-85, 0, 0], ShinR: [95, 0, 0], FootR: [35, 0, 0] });\nhold('Warrior', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.2, 0] }, Torso: [0, 25, 0], Head: [0, 40, 0], ArmR: [0, 0, -90], ArmL: [0, 0, 90] }, { z: 0.38 }, { z: -0.38 }));\nhold('Chair', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.28, -0.06] }, Torso: [24, 0, 0], Head: [-18, 0, 0], ArmR: [-110, 0, -8], ArmL: [-110, 0, 8] }, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 }));\nhold('Fold', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.03, -0.03] }, Torso: [88, 0, 0], Head: [10, 0, 0], ArmR: [-70, 0, -6], ArmL: [-70, 0, 6], ForearmR: [-8, 0, 0], ForearmL: [-8, 0, 0] }, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 }));\nhold('Plank', { Pelvis: { r: [66, 0, 0], p: [0, -0.2, 0] }, Head: [-48, 0, 0], ArmR: [-63, 0, -5], ArmL: [-63, 0, 5], HandR: [-40, 0, 0], HandL: [-40, 0, 0], FootR: [55, 0, 0], FootL: [55, 0, 0] });\n// Scrubbed reps: keys built with placeFeet AND a feet track, or the sole dips through the floor mid-clip.\nconst squatTop = { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.02, 0] }, Torso: [2, 0, 0], ArmR: [6, 0, -9], ArmL: [6, 0, 9] }, squatLow = { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.3, -0.05] }, Torso: [26, 0, 0], Head: [-20, 0, 0], ArmR: [-85, 0, -8], ArmL: [-85, 0, 8] };\n({ name: 'SquatRep', frames: 30, grounded: true, keys: [[0, feet(squatTop, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 })], [30, feet(squatLow, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 })]], feet: [[0, { R: { z: 0 }, L: { z: 0 } }], [30, { R: { z: 0 }, L: { z: 0 } }]] });\n// LungeRep: the same way, low pose Pelvis p [0,-0.24,0], Torso [6,0,0], goals R { z: .34 }, L { z: -.32, pitch: 25, pivot: 'ball' }. For the left side, map poses through mirror(pose, HERO_RIG) and swap R and L goals.\n```\n\n**Still to author:** Press; StepL/StepR; header nod; flail; daze; bow; slow clap; sneeze; Coach's point and demonstration transitions; tuck and cannonball; judge raising a paddle; stepping onto Ounce; ferry disembark. Reuse kit clips: `Idle`, `Walk`, `Run`, `Sit`, `LieIdle`, `Wave`, `Victory`, `Teeter`, `Hurt`, `Fall`, `GetUp`, and more (`HERO_CLIPS`).\n\n**Preview without a GPU ✔:** `tools/clip-sheet.mjs` uses `renderSheet(model, HERO_RIG, def, clip, { frames, views: ['front', 'side'], scale: 90, trails: false, skeleton: false })` → `{ width, height, data }`, written as a PNG with `node:zlib` (`deflateSync`, `crc32`). Look at every new pose once. Hide the hat and moustache first so you judge the real silhouette.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Audio\n\nEverything is written in code. No audio files.\n\n### Music\n\n- **`ctx.audio.setVolume('music', savedMusic ?? 0.10)` at boot, every boot**, from your own settings key. The engine's default is 60%, and its stored volume key (`pixel-engine:audio`) is shared by every engine game on the origin, so don't rely on it.\n- **Write instruments loud:** track `volume` 0.45-0.8. The kit's examples use about 0.12, written for a 60% bus; at 10% × master .8 that is near silence. A test checks each song: sum of track volumes × 0.1 × 0.8 ≥ 0.03.\n- Songs are `Song` data, in `src/audio/songs.js`, each original, none imitating the source:\n\n| Song | Feel |\n|---|---|\n| Title / Plaza | gentle waiting-room bossa, about 92 BPM, soft triangle plucks |\n| Holding Still | slow, sparse, breath-paced, 60 BPM |\n| Rep Shed | light funk bass, 110 BPM |\n| Beat Beach (Hoop) and Step Class | bright, four-on-the-floor; Step is 104 BPM exactly |\n| Lagoon Games | staccato ukulele feel, 120 BPM |\n| Jog | steady, cheerful, 112 BPM |\n| Evening Report | music box, 70 BPM |\n| Long Stand | near silence, then one swelling chord line at t = 75 |\n\n### SFX\n\n`ctx.audio.register` data: needle tick, ring chime in/out, wobble warning, rep tick, step perfect/good, combo, coconut bonk, flip-flop thwap, hoop whirr (`loop`), splash, gust, gull squawk, jar drip, star pop, menu move/confirm/back, \"Ow\" stinger.\n\n### Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish\n\nBuild in `src/audio/voice.js`:\n\n1. **`syllabify(text, speaker)` is pure and testable in Node.** Words split into syllables; a hash of each word picks consonant class and vowel, so **the same word always sounds the same**. Output: `[{ t, dur, f0, vowel, cons, charIndex }]`. Declination -15% across a sentence; `?` rises 25% at the end; `!` +15%; `...` slows. The dialogue typewriter reads `charIndex`.\n2. **`renderVoice(ctx, destination, syllables, when)`** schedules, per syllable: a saw oscillator at `f0` through two parallel bandpass filters at the vowel's formants (a 800/1200, e 500/1900, i 300/2300, o 500/900, u 350/800, × speaker shift), gain envelope 6 ms up, 30 ms down; a noise burst for plosives (8 ms) and fricatives (40 ms).\n3. **Routing:** it works on any `BaseAudioContext`, so it renders in `OfflineAudioContext` for tests. Live, use `ctx.audio.context`, connected to `ctx.audio.buses.sfx` (undocumented but present in 0.46.0, so master and mute apply) via your own Voice gain. `ctx.audio.context` is null headless and before the first input: no-op and log.\n\n| Speaker | f0 | Syllables/s | Formant shift | Extra |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Ounce | 340 | 13 | ×1.25 | a needle tick on punctuation |\n| Coach | 165 | 7.5 | ×.9 | flat pitch, long pauses |\n| Marguerite | 230 | 9 | ×1 | slight vibrato |\n| Dennis | 120 | 11 | ×.95 | pitch up on last word |\n| June | 300 | 10 | ×1.15 | no contour at all |\n| Kevin | | | | squawk SFX, never words |\n\n---\n\n## 16. Architecture","numLines":90,"startLine":672,"totalLines":993}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Pb7JwcKyiTqAQXc4xkxctg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
