{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D2hokXmk7TSQmRsJ2Mb6UW","type":"tool_result","content":"7a1dc7d23b6c7fe4\n== TASK.md on this machine's limits\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n\n### Sharing this computer\n\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the brow\n== PLAN wording\nYou are the builder. Build this game from this plan and your brief. Nobody will answer questions, so where the plan leaves something open, decide and move on.\n| Place | Near (x, z) | Purpose |\n| Scenery | | Kettlebell Volcano (-15, -14), Foam Roller Hills (15, -14), Dumbbell Bridge over an inlet, medicine balls,\n18. Audio after a real click: an `AnalyserNode` on the destination reads non-silent for SFX and music; voice in `OfflineAudioContext` has RMS > .02, and Ounce's mean pitch exceeds Coach's.\nslackline idle: finished 0/3 \nslackline sloppy: finished 0/6 \nslackline average: finished 10/10 mean 40.6 s, falls 0.40\nslackline good: finished 6/6 mean 28.6 s, falls 0.00\n2 s a line: weigh-in 39.4 33.5 34.1; report 17.1 16.8 16.8\n3 s a line: weigh-in 44.6 38.6 38.9; report 19.1 18.8 18.8\n4 s a line: weigh-in 50.6 43.6 43.9; report 21.1 20.8 20.8\nfull-size volcano skirt radius 7 m; its centre at the plan spot is 5.0 m from the Lagoon station at (-12,-10)\n(clean)\n7a1dc7d23b6c7fe4","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2ae2eb7-ae7f-44a8-ac16-77fd998e0107","uuid":"dd39c8a1-d092-43d1-bf70-fcbff2ae82ec","timestamp":"2026-11-05T10:30:44.050Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"7a1dc7d23b6c7fe4\n== TASK.md on this machine's limits\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n\n### Sharing this computer\n\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the brow\n== PLAN wording\nYou are the builder. Build this game from this plan and your brief. Nobody will answer questions, so where the plan leaves something open, decide and move on.\n| Place | Near (x, z) | Purpose |\n| Scenery | | Kettlebell Volcano (-15, -14), Foam Roller Hills (15, -14), Dumbbell Bridge over an inlet, medicine balls,\n18. Audio after a real click: an `AnalyserNode` on the destination reads non-silent for SFX and music; voice in `OfflineAudioContext` has RMS > .02, and Ounce's mean pitch exceeds Coach's.\nslackline idle: finished 0/3 \nslackline sloppy: finished 0/6 \nslackline average: finished 10/10 mean 40.6 s, falls 0.40\nslackline good: finished 6/6 mean 28.6 s, falls 0.00\n2 s a line: weigh-in 39.4 33.5 34.1; report 17.1 16.8 16.8\n3 s a line: weigh-in 44.6 38.6 38.9; report 19.1 18.8 18.8\n4 s a line: weigh-in 50.6 43.6 43.9; report 21.1 20.8 20.8\nfull-size volcano skirt radius 7 m; its centre at the plan spot is 5.0 m from the Lagoon station at (-12,-10)\n(clean)\n7a1dc7d23b6c7fe4","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01D2hokXmk7TSQmRsJ2Mb6UW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
